Page 24 A: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|tl|es|A}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der|tl|en|A}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by [[Baybayin]] character {{m|tl|ᜀ}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der|tl|es|A}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name|Filipino alphabet}} {{IPA|tl|/ˈʔej/|[ˈʔɛɪ̯]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA}} -->
* {{sense|letter name|Abakada alphabet|Abecedario}} {{IPA|tl|/ˈʔa/|[ˈʔɐ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA}} -->
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|tl|/a/|[ɐ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA}} -->
* {{rhymes|tl|ej|a|s=1}}

===Letter===
{{head|tl|letters|upper case||lower case|a|Baybayin spelling|ᜁᜌ᜔|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def|tl|letter|1|ey|alphabet name={{w|Filipino alphabet}}}}

===Letter===
{{head|tl|letters|upper case||lower case|a|Baybayin spelling|ᜀ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def|tl|letter|1|a|alphabet name={{w|Abakada alphabet}}}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def|tl|letter|1|a|alphabet name={{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}}}

====See also====
* {{list:Latin script letters/tl/simple}}

-------- end text --------
Page 25 a: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|tl|es|a}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der|tl|en|a}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by [[Baybayin]] character {{m|tl|ᜀ}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der|tl|es|a}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|letter name|Filipino alphabet}} {{IPA|tl|/ˈʔej/|[ˈʔɛɪ̯]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA}} -->
* {{sense|letter name|Abakada alphabet|Abecedario}} {{IPA|tl|/ˈʔa/|[ˈʔɐ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA}} -->
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|tl|/a/|[ɐ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA}} -->
* {{rhymes|tl|ej|a|s=1}}

====Letter====
{{head|tl|letter|lower case||upper case|A|Baybayin spelling|ᜁᜌ᜔|cat2=terms with Baybayin script|f3sc=Tglg}}

