From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*abala}}. Compare {{cog|pam|abala}}, {{cog|pag|abala}}, and {{cog|dgc|abala}}. Zorc (1979) posits the senses {{m-g|busy; preoccupied}} were {{bor+|tl|pag|abala|nocap=1}}, from {{der|tl|map-pro|*qabaʀa||shoulder}} with semantic shift.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|q1=noun|IPA2=abalá|q2=adjective}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[trouble]]; [[bother]]; [[inconvenience]]
#: {{syn|tl|gulo}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ang matagal na problema ng trapik sa mga kalsada ay isang matinding '''abala''' sa mamamayan.|The long-time problem of road traffic is a heavy '''burden''' to people.}}
# [[interruption]]; [[delay]]; [[disturbance]]
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[act]] of [[borrow]]ing from [[someone]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|abalahin|maabala|mang-abala|punong-abala|magpakaabala|makaabala}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|abalá|b=+}}

# [[busy]]; [[preoccupied]]; [[distracted]]
#: {{ux|tl|Wala akong oras dahil '''abala''' ako sa pangangalaga sa lolo ko.|I've no time because I'm '''busy''' taking care of my grandfather.}}
# [[absorbed]]; [[obsessed]]; [[engrossed]]; [[preoccupied]]
# [[inconvenient]]; [[bothersome]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''Abala''' naman ang pinagagawa mo sa akin.|What you're asking me to do is '''troublesome'''.}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|mag-abala|abalang-abala|mapag-abala}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:CEDOF|1|1}}
-------- end text --------
