Page 360 agimat: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|aguimat||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|tl|mdh|agimat|t=amulet; talisman}} or {{bor|tl|tsg|ajimat|t=amulet; talisman}}, from {{der|tl|ms|azimat|tr={{m|ms|عزيمة}}}}, from {{der|tl|ar|عَزِيمَة|tr=ʕazīmat}}, the informal {{w|construct state}} of {{m|ar|عزيمة|tr=ʕazīma}}. Compare {{cog|mrw|adimat}} and {{cog|tsg|adjimat}}.

The {{m-g|amulet; talisman}} sense is first attested in c. 1860 via Noceda & Sanlucar, with the term arriving in the Philippines in the first half of the 1800s according to Potet (2013), while the homophonous "thrift; care" sense is attested since c. 1754 also via Noceda & Sanlucar according to Potet (2013). See also {{cog|ms|jimat||frugal; prudent; saving money}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[amulet]]; [[talisman]]; [[charm]]
#: {{syn|tl|anting-anting|galing|dupil}}
# {{lb|tl|slang}} [[methamphetamine]]; [[crystal meth]]
#: {{syn|tl|bato|shabu}}
# [[care]]; [[concern]]
# [[anxiety]]; [[worry]]
# {{lb|tl|formerly|_|obsolete|now|neologism}} [[thrift]]; [[economy]]
#: {{syn|tl|pagtitipid|pag-iimpok}}

