Page 585 alaska: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Root word of {{m|tl|alaskador||one who loves to tease people}}, with the etymology uncertain. The old meaning may have referred to {{m-g|someone who always wants to be above others}}, coined from the catchphrase of the milk-producing company {{w|Alaska}},  with tagline {{m-g|Wala pa ring tatalo sa Alaska}}, {{lit|Still, no one can beat Alaska|nocap=1}}. This meaning being associated with boastfulness and condescension made its sense shift to the current meaning.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|hmp=Alaska}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|slang}}

# act of [[tease|teasing]], [[make fun of|making fun of]], [[ridicule|riduculing]], or [[vex]]ing
#: {{syn|tl|asar}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|tl|pang-aalaska|nang-aalaska|alaskahin}}
-------- end text --------
Page 586 alaskador: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|tl|alaska|dor}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|alaskadór}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|alaskadór|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|slang}}

# [[teaser]]; a person who likes to [[tease]]
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1989|author=Reuel Molina Aguila|title=Ligalig, at iba pang dula|isbn=9789718577295
|passage=REY. '''Alaskador''' ka pa rin. DOM. No, tell me,  Rey. Bumusina ka lang kung nasasaktan na kita.
|t=REY. You're also a teaser. No, tell me, Rey. Tell me only if I've already hurt you.}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1997|title=Pulang hamtik
|passage=Sabi nga ng mga kasama niya, '''alaskador''' kasi si Ka Vito, kaya pati usapin ng kamatayan ay inaalaska pa rin. Alaskador. ... ito ang trademark niya sa kilusan.
|translation=What his friends said is that Vito is an teaser, so [he] still tries to poke fun on the topic of death. ''Alaskador'' [teaser] is his trademark in the movement.}}
-------- end text --------
