====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|amá}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|amá|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|Chinese Filipino|colloquial}}

# [[paternal]] [[grandmother]]; [[paternal]] [[grandma]]
#: {{syn|tl|lola}}
#: {{coord|tl|angkong}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2006|author=Christine S. Bellen|editors=Carla M. Pacis; Eugene Y. Evasco|publisher=UP Press|title=Bagets: an anthology of Filipino young adult fiction|chapter=Trese|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=7d1FOdaBfhQC&pg=PA12&dq=angkong&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiR9eu0xLn7AhUSbd4KHfK-Dj8Q6AF6BAgDEAI#v=onepage&q=ama&f=false|page=11|text=Mestisang Tsina naman si Nanay. Negosyante sina '''Ama''' at Angkong ko. Purong Tsino si Angkong. Lumikas mula sa Macao ang pamilya nila at dito sa Pilipinas nagtayo ng isang maliit na tindahan hanggang sa lumago ito at naging isang grocery.|t=Mom is a Chinese mestiza. My '''grandmother''' and grandfather are businesspeople. Grandpa is a pure Chinese. Their family evacuated from Macau and it was here in the Philippines where they started a small store until it flourished and became a grocery.}}
# {{n-g|[[term of address]] for one's paternal grandmother}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2006|author=Christine S. Bellen|editors=Carla M. Pacis; Eugene Y. Evasco|publisher=UP Press|title=Bagets: an anthology of Filipino young adult fiction|chapter=Trese|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=7d1FOdaBfhQC&pg=PA12&dq=angkong&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiR9eu0xLn7AhUSbd4KHfK-Dj8Q6AF6BAgDEAI#v=onepage&q=ama&f=false|page=11|text=Sa Pilipinas na napangasawa ni Angkong si '''Ama'''. Pilipina ang nanay ni '''Ama''' pero sila ang mas mahigpit sa mga pamahiing Tsino.|t=It was in the Philippines already where Grandpa married '''Grandma'''. '''Grandma's''' mother is a Filipina but they are the ones who are stricter in Chinese superstitions.}}

