===Etymology===
From {{compound|tl|ama|ng|sinaya}}, {{lit|father of the first catch|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|Amánsináya|IPA2=Amánsináyà}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|Amánsináya|head2=Amánsinayà|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|mythology}}

#  [[ancient]] [[pagan]] [[god]] of [[fishermen]]

====Usage notes====
* According to Potet (2017), '''''Amansinaya''''' was mistakenly perceived to be female because of the final ''-a'' associated with Spanish feminine ending ''-a'' similar to how {{m|tl|ginoo}} was mistaken to be male because of the word ending with ''-o''.

