Page 901 anak ng tinapa: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|son of a smoked fish}}, originally uttered by smoked fish makers.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|anák ng tinapá}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|[[anák]] [[ng]] [[tinapá]]|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|idiom}} {{n-g|an expression of shock or amazement}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2011|author=Romeo “Choppy” Vargas|title=THE MAKING OF THE PORKCHOP DUO: An Autobiographical Joke Book The Philippine’s Wackiest Comedy Duo|publisher=Xlibris Corporation|isbn=9781462884346
|passage=“'''Anak ng tinapa''', hoy, huwag ninyo munang ipaflush!” “Ngeee!” I graduated  from Isabelo delos Reyes Elementary School in 1965. Unlike other kids my age, I  didn&#39;t go to high school in the morning. I couldn&#39;t go to school in the afternoon  either&nbsp;...|t="'''Son of a smoked fish''', hey, don't you all flush yet!" "Ngeee!" I graduated  from Isabelo delos Reyes Elementary School in 1965. Unlike other kids my age, I  didn&#39;t go to high school in the morning. I couldn&#39;t go to school in the afternoon  either&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1997|author=Cecilia Manguerra Brainard|title=Contemporary fiction by Filipinos in America|publisher=Anvil Pub Inc|isbn=9789712707018
|passage='''Anak ng tinapa'''. The families just couldn&#39;t cope and turned their sons away!  Steven said I was his brown Ganymede, always pouring sweet wine into his  silver chalice. It was like Mitchell all over again. This time though, the wine aged  for six&nbsp;...|t='''Son of a smoked fish'''. The families just couldn&#39;t cope and turned their sons away!  Steven said I was his brown Ganymede, always pouring sweet wine into his  silver chalice. It was like Mitchell all over again. This time though, the wine aged  for six&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=2001|author=Philippine Social Science Council|title=Philippine Social Science Council Social Science Information
|passage=But for crying out loud . . . you know, anong term in the vernacular, '''Anak ng  tinapa''' naman, hindi nyo pa nakikita ang problemang ito? My goodness! This is  really the situation we are in. And I just cannot believe that we are not acting on it  at all.|t=But for crying out loud . . . you know, anong term in the vernacular, What a '''son of a smoked fish''', you all haven't seen this problem? My goodness! This is  really the situation we are in. And I just cannot believe that we are not acting on it  at all.}}
-------- end text --------
Page 902 anak ng tipaklong: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Minced oath of {{m|tl|anak ng puta}}, {{lit|son of a grasshopper|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|anák ng tipaklóng}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|[[anák]] [[ng]] [[tipaklóng]]|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|minced oath}} {{n-g|an expression of annoyance}}
#: {{syn|tl|anak ng puta|anak ng tokwa|anak ng tupa}}
#* '''2003''', Ben Villar Condino, ''Puera biro: at iba pang katha''
#*: REKLAMO NI MISIS ANG SANHI NG BAGONG KRISIS '''Anak ng Tipaklong'''! Lekat!  Salamabits! Sa aming tahanan ay may Bagong Krisis! Mangyari, kagabi&#39;y nag- Alma si Misis, Halatang Asar na sa Tono ng Boses . . . Ang puno at dulo ng&nbsp;...anak ng tokwa|
