From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*hapuy}} (compare {{cog|ch|guåfi}}, {{cog|haw|ahi}}, {{cog|ms|api}}, {{cog|mi|ahi}}, and {{cog|sm|afi}}), from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*Sapuy}} (compare {{cog|pwn|sapuy}}), possibly through a borrowing from Dumagat, Sambal, etc., since evidence indicates that one would expect ''*hapoy'' in Tagalog, according to Zorc.

