Page 1776 bahala ka: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{m|tl|bahala||responsibility}} and {{m|tl|ka||you}}. {{lit|you (are with) [[burden]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|bahala7 ka}}
* {{hyph|tl|ba|ha|la|ka}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|[[bahalà]] [[ka]]|b=+}}

# {{n-g|expresses the desire to not be involved, and to leave the situation to the second person}}: it's up to you; you're on your own; do what you want
#: {{ux|tl|''Tulungan mo naman ako. — '''Bahala ka'''!''|''Help me, please. — '''You're on your own'''!''}}
#: {{ux|tl|''Anong oras ba dapat ako dadating sa party mo? — '''Bahala ka'''.''|''What time do I have to come to your party? — '''It's up to you'''.''}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|bahala|bahala na}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|bathala}}
-------- end text --------
Page 1777 bahala na: -------- begin text --------
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{ellipsis|tl|[[bahala]] [[ka]] [[na]]|t=you are with burden already|nocap=1}} where {{m|tl|ka|t=you}} is omitted, then [[Appendix:Glossary#contamination|conflated]] with {{m|tl|Bathala|t=the precolonial Supreme deity of the Tagalog people}}, which an expression was preconceived, {{m|tl|[[Bathala]] [[na]]|lit=(leave it to) God already}}. In this case, {{m|tl|bahala}} was preserved, but the notion remained that it was short for {{m|tl|[[bahala]] [[na]] [[ang]] [[Diyos]]|t=God will take care of it; leave it to God|lit=burden already of God}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|bahala7 na}}
* {{hyph|tl|ba|ha|la|na}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|[[bahalà]] [[na]]|b=+}}

# {{n-g|expresses fatalistic resignation, optimistic acceptance, or plain indifference in an uncertain or difficult circumstance}}: [[come what may]]

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|bahala na si Bathala|bahala na si Batman}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|bahala|bahala ka}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|bathala}}
-------- end text --------
