===Etymology===
Borrowed from (c. 16th-18th century) {{w|Early Modern Spanish|Early Modern}} {{bor|tl|es|barajar||to shuffle}}, with loss of final {{IPAchar|/r/}} possibly through an [[inflection]] (see {{m|es|baraja}}), shift of stress to penultimate, change of intervocalic {{IPAchar|/r/}} to {{IPAchar|/l/}}, and Spanish {{angbr|j}}, then pronounced {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}}, became Tagalog {{IPAchar|/s/}} ({{IPAchar|/baɾaˈʃaɾ/}} → {{IPAchar|/baˈlasa/}}). Possibly also from {{cog|es|baraja||deck of cards}}. {{doublet|tl|baraha}}, a later borrowing from {{cog|es|baraja}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|ba|la|sa}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[shuffle]] {{gloss|act of shuffling cards}}
# [[reshuffle]]; [[reorganization]]
# [[shift]] of [[gait]] of a [[running]] [[horse]]

