Page 2157 bansa: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lbor+|tl|ms|bangsa}}, from {{der|tl|sa|वंश|tr=vaṃśá||offspring, lineage, collection}}, from {{der|tl|iir-pro|*wanćás||ceiling beam}}. Introduced by {{coinage|tl|Eusebio T. Daluz|w=-|in=the early 20th century|notext=1}} as counterpart to the [[Spanish]] ''{{l|es|nación|t=nation}}'', as it was deemed that there was no native Tagalog word that adequately expressed the concept, since the nearest counterpart, ''{{l|tl|bayan}}'', had other meanings that deviate from the modern concept of nationhood, as it is also used to refer to a {{l|en|town}} or a {{l|en|municipality}}, similar to [[Spanish]] ''{{l|es|pueblo}}''. However, usage of the word has preceded publications by Eusebio T. Daluz.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|bansá7,bansá|new=1}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|bansâ|head2=bansá|b=+}}

# [[nation]]
#: {{syn|tl|nasyon|bayan|pais|q3=rare}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1909|publisher=Philippine Teachers' Association|title=The Filipino Teacher Volume 3, Issue 3
|passage=Ang bayang itó ay di kaila sa alin mang kasaysayan na marami nang '''bansâ''' ang nagnanasang maghari dito at sa katunaya'y may ilan na ng̃ang nakapaghari. Ang Kastila, na nakapaghari dito na mahiguit sa tatlong daan taon ay siyá kong uunkatin.}}
# [[country]]
#: {{syn|tl|pais|q1=rare}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kabansaan|pagkabansa|isabansa|magsabansa|makabansa|Mga Nagkakaisang Bansa|pagkakasabansa|pagsasabansa|pambansa|pambansa-bansa|pamansaan|pakikipamansaan|Mga Bansang Pinagbuklod|wikang pambansa|Batasang Pambansa|pambansang seguridad|kapitbansa|pambansang awit}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
