===Noun===
{{tl-noun|basyó|b=+}}

# [[empty]] [[container]] {{gl|of bottles, cans, etc.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=tl
|year=1986
|author=Writers Union of the Philippines
|title=Mithi: literary journal of the Writers Union of the Philippines, Issues 13-15
|url=https://books.google.com/books?redir_esc=y&id=alK5AAAAIAAJ
|text=Ilang sandali pa, tatalikod muli si Fred at pupuluting isa-isa ang mga '''basyo''' ng beer.
|t=A few moments later, Fred will turn to his back and will pick up the '''empty''' beer bottles one by one.
}}
#* {{quote-book|1=tl|year=2017|author=J. Neil Garcia; Danton Remoto|title=Ladlad 2: An Anthology of Philippine Gay Writing|chapter=Dear Kuya Cesar (Nicolas B. Pichay)
|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=X76bDwAAQBAJ&redir_esc=y
|isbn=9789712733369
|text=Nagpuyat kami sa pagpapatayo ng piramid mula sa mga '''basyo''' ng pinag-inumang vodka tonic. Nabulabog ako sa umagang iyon. Sa mga katulad ko na hindi pa naimumumog ang panunuyo ng ngalangala, hindi magandang biro ang gisingin ng mga walang katuturang pang-aaliw.
|t=We stayed awake building a pyramid from '''empty''' bottles of vodka and tonic. I'm surprised that morning. On the likes of us who didn't gargled our dry palates, it's a bad idea to wake someone up with senseless entertainment.
}}
# {{lb|tl|firearms}} [[used]] [[cartridge]]

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|basyó|b=+}}

# [[empty]] {{gl|of containers}}
#: {{ant|tl|puno}}
#* {{quote-book|1=tl|year=2005|title=Edukasyong Pantahanan at Pangkabuhayan 5' 2005 Ed.
|url=https://books.google.com/books/about/Edukasyong_Pantahanan_at_Pangkabuhayan_5.html?id=QPsiMdKy5gkC&redir_esc=y
|page=112
|text=Magtatanim ako sa paso o sa mga '''basyong''' lata.
|t=I will plant it in a pot or in '''empty''' cans.
}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=tl|year=2015
|author=Epifanio San Juan, Jr.
|title=Panitikan, Ideolohiya, Rebolusyon: Edukasyon at Pedagohiya sa Pagbasa ng Nobelang Desaparasidos ni Lualhati Bautista
|journal=Daluyan: Journal ng Wikang Filipino
|url=https://journals.upd.edu.ph/index.php/djwf/article/view/4511
|page=219
|text=Awtoridad ang titser, kinatawan ng Estado at siyang nagdedeposito ng kaalaman sa '''basyong''' utak ng mga kabataan.
|t=The teacher is the authority, the representative of the State, and the one who fills with knowledge the '''empty''' minds of the children.
}}

