Page 2693 bihag: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*bihaʀ||captive: taken alive in war; to spare: allow to live}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|biag}}, {{cog|pag|bilay}}, {{cog|xsb|biyay}}, {{cog|pam|bie}}, {{cog|ceb|bihag}}, {{cog|mrw|biyag}} / {{m|mrw|oyag}}, and {{cog|ms|biar}}. Possible {{doublet|tl|buhay|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|q=noun|IPA2=bihág|q2=adjective}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[captive]]; [[prisoner]]
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[sprouting]] of a [[plant]]
#: {{syn|tl|sibol|usbong|tubo}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} act of [[live|living]] or letting something [[live]]
#: {{syn|tl|buhay}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Bihagin''' mo iyang baboy.|'''Let''' the pig '''live'''.}}
# {{lb|tl|physiology|figuratively|obsolete}} [[erection]] of a [[penis]]
#: {{syn|tl|ereksiyon|pagtayo|paninigas|katog|utog}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[life]] of an [[animal]] or [[plant]] {{defdate|16th|17th c.}}
#: {{syn|tl|buhay}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|bihagin|bumihag|mamihag|mabihag|mambibihag|mamimihag|mapamihag|pagbihag|pagkabihag|pagkakabihag|mambihag|kabihagan|magbihag|makabihag|pabihagin}}

