Page 2713 Bikol: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|Bicol}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|tl|es|Bicol}} / {{m|es|Vicol||former province, river ({{w|Bicol River}}), language}}, from either {{der|tl|bcl|bikolbikol||a tree species}} or {{m|bcl|biko||bent; twisted}}. Compare {{cog|tl|bikol||a species of hard tree}}, attested as ''"BICOL"/"bicol"'' in the ''Vocabulario de la lengua tagala'' (1860)<ref>{{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860|46}}</ref>

Named in the early [[Spanish]] records as ''Bicol'', ''Vicol'', ''Vicor'', ''Bico'', referring to the former province in the region and the {{w|Bicol River}}. It is believed to have come from {{m|bcl|biko|t=[[twisted]] or [[bent]]}} or it could also be from {{m|bcl|bikolbikol||timber producing tree species, also possessing a bark once used for making rope.}}, attested as ''BICOLBICOL'' in the ''Vocabulario de la lengua bicol'' (1865).<ref>{{cite-book|first=Marcos|last=de Lisboa|year=1865|title=Vocabulario de la lengua bicol|page=63|location=Manila|url=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=ucm.532528906x&view=1up&seq=67&q1=bicol}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|Bi|kol}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

