===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|bilango||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}} <ref>{{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860|48|'''BILANGÓ'''. pc. {{l|es|alguacil}}}}</ref>

===Etymology===
Borrowing from {{bor|tl|hil|bilanggo||prisoner; bailiff}} or from {{bor|tl|ceb|bilanggo}}.<ref name="William Henry Scott">{{cite-book|author=Scott, William Henry|chapter=The Visayas|title=Barangay: Sixteenth-century Philippine Culture and Society|year=1994|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books/about/Barangay.html?id=15KZU-yMuisC|page=70|publisher=Ateneo University Press|text=His sheriff or constable was ''bilanggo'', whose own house served as a jail, ''bilanggowan''{{sic}}.}}</ref> The Cebuano and Hiligaynon may have descended from Proto-Visayan *''bilaŋgu'', ultimately from {{der|tl|ta|விலங்கு|gloss=animal; fetters; shackles; manacles}}.<ref>{{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=302}}</ref> See also {{cog|ms|belenggu||shackle}}.

Sense 2, possibly from {{back-formation|tl|bilangguan||prison|nocap=1}} (borrowing from Cebuano or Hiligaynon {{m|ceb|bilanggoan}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|bilanggô}}
* {{hyph|tl|bi|lang|go}}

===Noun===
