Page 3122 budol: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From slang in {{bor|tl|hil|budol-budol||swindling; chubby; cute}}, an allusion to the {{w|List of gangs in the Philippines|Budol-Budol Gang}} which specializes in conning victims to give their money or possessions, possibly from {{der|tl|en|boodle||illegally acquired money}}. See also {{cog|akl|buroe||jellyfish}}, {{cog|krj|budul-budul||cute}}, {{ncog|hil|budol||jellyfish}} and {{m|hil|tibudol||fat}}. Also possibly a {{metathesis|tl}} of {{der|tl|en|double}}, possibly from {{m|en|double-cross}} according to Zorc (1993).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|bu|dol}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|slang}}

# [[act]] of [[cheating]], [[swindling]], or [[double-crossing]]
#: {{syn|tl|daya|loko|gantso}}
#: {{ux|tl|Siya ay '''budol''' ng mga manloloko.|He was '''cheated''' by scammers.}}
# act of [[persuading]], [[influencing]], or [[convincing]] someone into doing something
#: {{syn|tl|kumbinsi|impluwensiya|hikayat}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Budol''' niya ako na sumama sa kanya sa ''Halloween party''.|She '''convinced''' me to come with her to a Halloween party.}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension|humorous}} [[purchased]] [[goods]], especially those that were [[impulsive]], [[unplanned]] or [[unnecessary]]
#: {{ux|tl|Marami siyang '''budol''' mula sa tindahan ng bisikleta dahil sa kanyang matinding pagnanais na mag-''upgrade''.|He had a lot of '''impulse purchases''' from the bike shop because of his strong desire to make upgrades.}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|nabudol|mabudol|pambubudol|ibudol|mambubudol|mambudol}}

