Page 3726 charing: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{m|tl|Charing|t=female given name}}, from {{suffix|tl|Charito|-ng}}, where {{m|tl|Charito}} itself is from {{suffix|tl|Charo|-ito}}, originally {{der|tl|es|-}}. The cultured sense is influenced by {{bor|tl|en|charming}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|charíng}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|charíng|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|women's speech}}

# {{lb|tl|originally|_|gay slang}} {{n-g|expression by a speaker, playfully admitting to telling a [[joke]] or a [[lie]]}}: [[just kidding]] 
# {{lb|tl|gay slang}} {{n-g|expression of [[impatience]] or [[rejection]] towards one being spoken to}}: [[I've]] [[had]] [[enough]]!
#: {{syn|tl|tama na}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|charíng|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|women's speech}}

# {{lb|tl|slang}} [[flirtatious]]; [[loose]] {{gl|of a woman}}
#: {{syn|tl|malandi}}
# {{lb|tl|gay slang}} [[contrived]]; [[artificial]]

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|charíng|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|women's speech}}

# {{lb|tl|originally|_|gay slang}} [[joke]]; [[lie]]; [[fib]]
# {{lb|tl|gay slang}} [[homosexual]] [[male]]; [[gay]] {{gl|especially one who is soft, cultured, or sophisticated}}

====Usage notes====
* The word is typically used by [[women]], and may sound [[effeminate]] when used by [[men]].

