Page 3934 daigdig: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|daygdig||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|dayigdig|dayigrig||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From Greater Central Philippine ''*daləgdəg'' (“thunder”), ultimately from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*dəʀdəʀ||thunder}}. Cognate with {{cog|akl|daeugdog}}, {{cog|bno|rayugrog}}, {{cog|ceb|dalugdog}}, {{cog|mrw|dalendeg}}, {{cog|mdh|dalendeg}}, and {{cog|tsg|dawgdug}}. The current meaning comes from the ancient belief that thunder can be heard throughout the world, hence the term {{m|tl|sandaigdigan}}, now shortened as ''daigdig'', to refer to the entire world as a single area that the sound of thunder can reach.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|da7igdíg}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|daigdíg|b=+}}

# [[world]]; [[earth]]
#: {{syn|tl|mundo|sangkalupaan|sanlibutan|sandaigdigan|santinakpan|sansinukuban|sangkahilihiran|Lupa}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[sphere]] {{gl|of any human activity}}
#: {{syn|tl|larangan}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[soft]] [[thunder]]
#: {{syn|tl|kulog}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|daigdigan|sandaigdigan|hating-daigdig|pandaigdig|kadaigdigan|digmaang pandaigdig|Bagong Daigdig|Lumang Daigdig|Unang Digmaang Pandaigdig|Ikalawang Digmaang Pandaigdig|dumaigdig|pandaigdigan|dignayan|kabilang daigdig}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|hilihid}}

