Page 4510 dilawan: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|tl|dilaw|an|t1=yellow}}. The political senses are from the yellow color associated with the {{w|Liberal Party (Philippines)|Liberal Party of the Philippines}} and [[liberalism]] itself locally. Originally used by both left-wing and right-wing politicians to attack members of the Liberal Party back in the 1980s, but its usage has been revived under the Aquino and Duterte administrations.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|dilawán<v^>|+,dilawán<n,a^>|new=1}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|dilawán|dinilawan|dinidilawan|didilawan|b=+}}

# to be [[made]] [[yellow]]
# to be [[add]]ed some [[turmeric]] {{gl|in food}}

====Conjugation====
{{tl-infl-in-an|d|i|law|law|object}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|dilawán|head2=+|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|politics|sometimes|_|derogatory}} [[w:Liberal Party (Philippines)|Liberal Party]] [[supporter]] {{gl|especially the Aquino administrations}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|dilawán|head2=+|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|politics|sometimes|_|derogatory}} [[liberal]]; of the [[w:Liberal Party (Philippines)|Liberal Party]]
