===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|map-pro|*di-ni||here}}. The latter half of the word is possibly related to {{m|tl|iri}}/{{m|tl|ire}}/{{m|tl|idi}}. See also {{m|tl|ganiri}} and other Tagalog demonstrative pronouns. Meanwhile, the former half is possibly related to {{cog|ms|di}} and {{cog|id|di}} as a likely cognate. Compare {{cog|ceb|ini}}, {{cog|tsg|dī}}, and {{cog|ms|ini}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
{{tl-IPA|dine}} {{q|colloquial}}
