Page 4892 e: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|tl|es|e}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der|tl|en|e}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by the [[Baybayin]] character {{m|tl|ᜁ}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der|tl|es|e}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name|Filipino alphabet}} {{tl-IPA|i}}
* {{sense|letter name|Abakada alphabet|Abecedario}} {{tl-IPA|bullets=0}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|tl|/e/|[ɛ]}}
* {{rhymes|tl|i|e|s=1}}

===Letter===
{{head|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|E|Baybayin spelling|ᜁ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def|tl|letter|5|i|alphabet name={{w|Filipino alphabet}}}}
# {{Latn-def|tl|letter|5|e|alphabet name={{w|Abakada alphabet}}}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def|tl|letter|6|e|alphabet name={{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}}}

====See also====
* {{list:Latin script letters/tl/simple}}
* {{l|tl|ë}}

===Noun===
{{head|tl|nouns|Baybayin spelling|ᜁ|f1sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def|tl|name|E|e|nocap=0|dot=,}} ''in the {{w|Abakada alphabet}}.''
#: {{syn|tl|i|q1=in the Filipino alphabet}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def|tl|name|E|e|nocap=0|dot=,}} ''in the {{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}.''
#: {{syn|tl|i|q1=in the Filipino alphabet}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|ii}}

===Etymology 2===
Compare {{cog|es|eh}} and {{cog|en|eh}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|eh}}
* {{alt|tl|weh||dialectal}}

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA|e(ː)}}
* {{rhymes|tl|e|s=1}}

====Interjection====
{{head|tl|interjections|Baybayin spelling|ᜂ|f1sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}} {{tlb|tl|informal}}

# {{n-g|Used to [[acknowledge]] a [[statement]] or [[situation]]}}: [[well]]; [[so]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''E''', ganoon '''e'''!|'''Well''', it's like that!}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''E''', ano ngayon?|'''So''', what now?}}
#: {{ux|tl|Nandoon siya, '''e'''.|'''Well''', he/she was/is there.}}
# {{n-g|Used to [[rhetorically]] express [[surprise]] or [[suspicion]]}}: [[so]]; [[oh]]; [[well]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''E''', sino naman 'yun?|'''Oh so then''', who was that?}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''E''', ikaw lang din naman 'yun.|'''Well anyways''', that was also only just you.}}
# {{n-g|Used to express [[indignance]]}}: [[well]]; [[but]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''E''', hindi mo naman kinailangan gawin iyon.|'''But''', you didn't need to do that.}}
# {{n-g|Used to [[introduce]] the [[continuation]] of [[narration]] from a [[previous]] [[understood]] [[point]]}}: [[and]]; [[well]]; [[so]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''E''', magkano naman ito?|'''And''', how much is this one?}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|edi}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|tl|o}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

