Page 5381 g: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor-lite|tl|es|g}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der-lite|tl|en|g}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by Baybayin character {{m-lite|tl|ᜄ|sc=Tglg|tr=ga}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der-lite|tl|es|g}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{hyph-lite|tl|g}} <!-- {{hyph|tl|G}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Filipino alphabet}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/dji/|[d͡ʒɪ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|dyi}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Abakada alphabet}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/ɡa/|[ɡɐ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|ga}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Abecedario}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/he/|[hɛ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|he}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/ɡ/|[ɡ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|g}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme|intervocalic}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/ɡ/|[ɣ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|g}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme|followed by e or i|English unadapted loanwords}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/dj/|[d͡ʒ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|j}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme|followed by e or i|Spanish unadapted loanwords}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/h/|[h]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|h}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme|followed by e or i|Spanish unadapted loanwords|archaic}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/s/|[s]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|s}} -->
* {{rhymes-lite|tl|i|a|e|s=1}}

====Letter====
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|G|Baybayin spelling|ᜇ᜔ᜌᜒ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|7|dyi|alphabet name={{w|Filipino alphabet}}}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letters/tl}}

====Letter====
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|G|Baybayin spelling|ᜄ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|6|ga|alphabet name={{w|Abakada alphabet}}}}

====Letter====
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|G|Baybayin spelling|ᜑᜒ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|8|ge|alphabet name={{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}}}

