Page 5904 gunting: -------- begin text --------
[[Image:Nozyczki4.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1|an assortment of scissors]]

===Etymology===
[[File:汉代剪刀.jpg|thumb|[[scissors]] from the {{w|Han dynasty}} of ancient China]]
[[File:Iron scissors, E Han.JPG|thumb|{{w|Eastern Han dynasty}} (25 AD – 220 AD) [[iron]] [[scissors]] from ancient China]]
[[File:Scissors (Jian) with Clouds and Floral Scrolls LACMA M.2003.14.jpg|thumb|Early to Mid {{w|Tang dynasty}} (618 AD – 800 AD) [[silver]] [[scissors]] from medieval China]]
Likely from {{bor|tl|ms|gunting}}, ultimately likely a loan from some non-Austronesian source, such as {{der|tl|zh}}, according to Blust (2010–). Compare {{cog|bcl|gunting}}, {{cog|ceb|gunting}}, {{cog|hil|gunting}}, {{cog|lmy|gutti}}, and {{cog|msk|gonting}} and {{cog|tsg|gunting}}.
 
Manuel (1948) also wondered about {{m|tl|gunting}} if it is from {{der|tl|zh|-}} or originally traces back to {{ncog|map-pro|-}}, which Dr. Cecilio Lopez stoutly affirmed from {{w|Otto Dempwolff|Dempwolff}}'s findings, although problems arose as the word is not found in the languages of the {{w|Igorot}} groups, which the only tenable conclusion was that {{m|tl|gunting}} is not originally from {{ncog|map-pro|-}} but instead from {{m-g|Southeastern Chinese}} (see {{w|Min Chinese}} languages, including {{ncog|nan-hbl|-}}) which had a term for scissors from which most probably the original term was derived from.

{{rfe|tl|Possibly {{ncog|nan-hbl|銀剪|tr=gûn-chián}}}}

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|guntíng}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|guntíng|b=+}}

# [[scissors]]
#: {{syn|tl|panggupit}}
# [[shears]]; [[big]] [[scissors]]
# [[cutting]] with [[scissors]] or [[shears]]
#: {{syn|tl|paggupit}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|guntingin|paggunting|gugunting}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|gupit|pasak}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:map:ACD|scissors|guntiŋ|type=lo|id=29931}}
* {{R:tl:Manuel 1948|q=scissors|pages=70-75}}

{{C|tl|Tools|Rock paper scissors}}

-------- end text --------
