Page 5912 guro: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lbor+|tl|ms|guru||teacher; educator}}, ultimately from {{derived|tl|sa|गुरु|tr=gurú}}. Reintroduced by {{coinage|tl|Eusebio T. Daluz|w=-|in=the early 20th century|notext=1}} as a replacement to the previously used words ''{{l|tl|maestro}}'' and ''{{l|tl|maestra}}'', both of [[Spanish]] origin. {{doublet|tl|gulo}}, another term from {{cog|ms|guru}}, that become obsolete in the course of the 19th century. Compare {{cog|en|guru}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|gurò|IPA2=gurô}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|gurò|head2=gurô|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|education}}

# [[teacher]]; [[educator]]; [[instructor]]
#: {{syn|tl|maestro|maestra|titser|tagapagturo|edukador|pedagogo}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|punong-guro|dalubguro|kaguruan|ulong-guro|kaguro}}

===Further reading===
