* The letter usually written an {{angbr|n}} before it,  For example: ''ba'''ng̃'''o'' ({{m|tl|bango}}, “fragrance”). However, the letter can also stand by itself as in ''ba'''g̃'''o''.
* Without the tilde, the {{angbr|ng}} will be understood as {{IPAchar|/ŋɡ/}} in the Spanish-based orthography and can be interpreted differently. For example, the difference between ''man'''g̃'''a'' ({{m|tl|manga}}/{{m|tl|mga}}, “plural marker”) and ''man'''g'''a'' ({{m|tl|mangga}}, “mango”). Although, in rare instances, {{angbr|g̃g}} can be found written together for {{IPAchar|/ŋɡ/}} as in: ''ma'''g̃g'''a''.
