Page 5945 h: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor-lite|tl|es|h}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der-lite|tl|en|h}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by Baybayin character {{m-lite|tl|ᜑ|sc=Tglg|tr=ha}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der-lite|tl|es|h}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyph-lite|tl|h}} <!-- {{hyph|tl|h}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Filipino alphabet}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/ˈʔejt͡ʃ/|[ˈʔɛɪ̯t͡ʃ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|eyts}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Abakada alphabet}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/ha/|[hɐ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|ha}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Abecedario}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/ˈʔat͡ʃe/|[ˈʔa.t͡ʃɛ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|atse}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/h/|[h]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|h}} --> {{q-lite|silent in Spanish unadapted loanwords}}
* {{rhymes-lite|tl|ejtʃ|a|atʃe|s1=1|s2=1|s3=2}}

===Letter===
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|H|Baybayin spelling|ᜁᜌ᜔ᜆ᜔ᜐ᜔|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

