===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr}}

===Etymology 1===
Unknown. Possibly from:
* {{bor|tl|nan-hbl|哈|tr=hâⁿ}} or {{m|nan-hbl|乎|tr=hôⁿ / hô͘}}, according to Manuel (1948)
* {{bor|tl|en|huh}}''?'' and {{bor|tl|en|hah}}''!''.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|ah}}
* {{alt|tl|a}}

====Interjection====
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|[[interrogative]] particle, used to express inquiry}}
#: {{syn|tl|[[ano]]?|t1=[[what]]?|[[po]]?|[[ho]]?}}
# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|[[speculative]] particle, used to express doubt, disbelief}}
#: {{syn|tl|[[ano]]?!|t1=[[what]]?!|a|alt2=a?! / ah?!}}
# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|[[exclamatory]] particle, used to express wonder, surprise, excitement}}
#: {{syn|tl|a|alt1=a! / ah!}}
# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|[[imperative]] [[final]] [[particle]], used to [[soften]] [[request]]s or [[command]]s to [[have]] someone [[do]] something}}
#: {{ux|tl|Ganoon, '''ha'''?!|Like that, '''ok'''?!}}
#: {{ux|tl|Kain ka na, '''ha'''.|Eat already, '''please'''.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Tulog na, '''ha'''?|Sleep already, '''will you'''?}}

===Etymology 2===
Influenced by Baybayin character {{m-lite|tl|{{tl-bay sc|ha}}|sc=Tglg}}.

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|name|H|h|dot=,}} ''in the {{w|Abakada alphabet}}.''
#: {{syn-lite|tl|eyts|hache|q1=in the Filipino alphabet|q2=in the Abecedario}}

