Page 6212 hatdog: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|en|hotdog}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|hat|dog}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|sometimes|humorous}} [[hotdog]]
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[bolster]]
#: {{syn|tl|dantayan|abrasador}}
# {{lb|tl|euphemism|slang}} [[penis]]; [[phallus]]
#: {{syn|tl|titi|ari}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|longganisa}}
* {{l|tl|tsoriso}}
* {{l|tl|batutay}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}}

# {{n-g|a nonsensical response to a question, specially the interjection {{l|tl|ha|ha?}}}}

====Usage notes====
* This can be used when the speaker does not want to answer the question.
* The response can be replaced by any words that start with ''ha'', more popularly, {{l|tl|halaman||plant}} as a replacement.
* A method for other question words, such as {{l|tl|saan||where}}, would be to find a word that has a similar first syllable of the question word, such as {{l|tl|sandok||ladle}}, e.g.
*: {{uxi|tl|Saan? sandok!|-}}
*; using {{l|tl|ano||what}}, in areas where the surname or place {{l|tl|Anonas}} is known
*: {{uxi|tl|Ano? Anonas!|-}}
* This may be considered [[dated]].

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|hakdog}}

{{C|tl|Sausages|Bedding|Genitalia}}
