===Etymology===
Possibly from {{af|tl|hin-||alt2=*diki|nocat=1}}, with initial {{glossary|reduplication}}. Compare {{cog|tsg|duku'-duku'||joke with or tease (someone)}}, {{noncog|id|dekih||chuckle, snigger, snicker}}, and {{ncog|ms|dekah||loud laughter}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|hindirikî}}
* {{hyph|tl|hin|di|ri|ki}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|hindirikî|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|obsolete}}

# [[play]]ing with a [[baby]] while [[carry]]ing it and [[pretend]]ing to [[tickle]] it to make it [[laugh]] {{defdate|18th|19th c.}}
# [[tickle|tickling]] all over the [[body]] {{defdate|16th|17th c.}}

====Usage notes====
* Fr. Domingo de los Santos (1835) provided an illustration of playing with a child wherein feet are played with the palms.

