Page 6572 hoy: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|huy|oy|uy}}

===Etymology===
Probably a natural expression, as may be inferred from its presence with similar meaning in many other unrelated languages: {{cog|en|hey}}, {{cog|cmn|哎|tr=āi}}, {{cog|la|eia}}, and {{cog|cs|ahoj}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}

===Interjection===
{{tl-head|interjection|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|colloquial|informal}} {{n-g|expression used to call the attention of somebody}}: [[hey]]!
#: {{ux|tl|'''Hoy'''! Gumising na kayong lahat dyan!|'''Hey'''! Wake up all of you there!}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial|informal}} {{n-g|expression used as a warning or as a protest}}: [[hey]]!
#: {{ux|tl|'''Hoy'''! Hindi ako ang kumuha ng pera mo!|'''Hey'''! I didn't take your money!}}

====Usage notes====
* The expression '''hoy''' can be perceived as disrespectful in some contexts, especially with one's seniors or superiors. Reactions may be heard such as:
*: {{uxi|tl|Huwag mo akong hoy-hoyin!|Don't call me 'hoy'!}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|hoy-hoyin}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|tuwan}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
