===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|tl|nan-hbl|番仔|tr=hoan-á}}, attested in the ''Dictionario Hispanico Sinicum'' (1626-1642) published in Manila, translated with {{ncog|es|indio|Yndio|t=native of the {{w|East Indies}}}}. Compare {{cog|id|huana}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA|Huwaná}}
* {{hyph|tl|Hu|wa|na}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|Huwaná|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|Chinese Filipino|colloquial|sometimes|vulgar}}

# [[Filipino]] of [[native]] or [[non]]-[[Chinese]] [[descent]] {{gl|as opposed to a Filipino of ethnic Chinese descent or an ethnic Chinese}}
#: {{coord|tl|Tsinoy|Intsik|Tsekwa|Sanglay|Tsino|tsinito|tsinita}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Some speakers, especially some {{w|Chinese Filipino}}s, consider this word as crude and vulgar, comparable to the perception of the word {{m|tl|Intsik|t=Chinese}}. It can be used [[neutrally]] or [[condescendingly]] based on context by the speaker's own intentions, whether positively, neutrally, or negatively. See {{w|Philippine Hokkien|Philippine}} {{ncog|nan-hbl|上番|tr=siōng-hoan}}, {{m|nan-hbl|番仔|tr=hoan-á}}, {{m|nan-hbl|臭番|tr=chhàu-hoan}}. Compare social dynamics with {{cog|id|huana}}, which has similar usage and social issues.

