Page 6711 huweteng: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|hueteng}}
* {{alt|tl|hweteng}}
* {{alt|tl|jueteng}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|tl|nan-hbl|-}},<ref name="Sawikaan"/> specifically {{bor|tl|nan-qua|花當|tr=hoe-tǹg}} as per:<ref name="Zorc"/>
* {{m|nan-hbl|買|tr=bóe|t=to buy; to purchase}} + {{m|nan-hbl|花當|tr=hoe-tǹg}} as per Douglas (1873/1899).<ref>{{R:nan:Douglas|hoe-hē|124}}</ref><ref>{{R:nan:Douglas|bóe-hoe-tǹg|147}}</ref><ref>{{R:nan:Douglas|bóe hoe-tǹg|512}}</ref>
* {{m|nan-hbl|花|tr=hoe|t=to spend|lit=flower; to bloom; to blossom}} + {{m|nan-hbl|當|tr=tǹg|t=to [[pawn]]; to take on [[mortgage]]}} according to Manuel (1948).<ref name="Manuel"/>
* {{m|nan-hbl|花|tr=hoe|t=to spend|lit=flower; to bloom; to blossom}} + {{m|nan-hbl|檔|tr=tòng|t=[[space]]}} according to Chan-Yap (1977) while transcribing the latter character as ⟨“tn”⟩.<ref name="Chan-Yap 1977"/> Though in Chan-Yap (1980), she transcribed the latter instead as ⟨“tŋ̣̆”⟩ ({{w|Pe̍h-ōe-jī|POJ}}: ''tǹg'') with a different character, {{m|nan-hbl|擋|tr=tòng}}.<ref name="Chan-Yap 1980"/> However, Chinese publications in the Philippines currently use {{zh-l|花檔}} to refer to the game.<ref name="PDSC"/><ref name="Phoenix TV"/> According to ({{zh-ref|Wang, 1982}}), {{m|nan-hbl|擋}} used to be written as {{m|nan-hbl|當}}.
The [[gambling]] [[game]] traces back to [[China]] where it is known more popularly and historically as [[花會]] and has been played since Early {{w|Ming Dynasty}} to Late {{w|Qing Dynasty}} times starting in Coastal China, specifically in [[Fujian]], [[Guangdong]], [[Guangxi]], [[Shanghai]], [[Zhejiang]], [[Jiangsu]], [[Tianjin]], [[Beijing]], and spreading across Inland [[China]] and [[abroad]] and finally banned last in [[China]] since 1949.<ref>{{cite-web|date=January 8, 2018|title=清末明初的另類彩票——打花會|trans-title=An Alternative Lottery Ticket in the Early Ming Dynasty and Late Qing Dynasty - To Play [[花會]]|work=每日頭條|trans-work=KK News Daily Headlines|url=https://kknews.cc/history/xvbbyyo.html}}</ref> It has been made [[illegal]] in the [[Philippines]] in 1907 under {{w|History of the Philippines (1898–1946)|American rule}}. In the 21st century, it is still played illegally [[in secret]] in [[China]] and the [[Philippines]] under the {{w|informal economy}} of both countries, but government-run lotteries are used to regulate and compete against the illegal private practice.<br>
See also {{m|tl|wahoy}} with {{ncog|nan-zha|花會|tr=hoa-hōe}} and {{ncog|nan-xia|花會|tr=hoe-hē}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
{{tl-IPA|weteng}} {{q|colloquial}}
* {{hyph|tl|hu|we|teng}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|gambling}} [[jueteng]] {{gl|an [[illegal]] [[Chinese]] [[numbers game]] [[lottery]] of number pairs from 1 to 37 on [[ball]]s or [[raffle]] [[ticket]] [[paper]]s stored in either a [[tambiolo]] container which is [[spun]] or a [[bottle]]-shaped or small-necked [[phial]] [[receptacle]] which is [[shaken]], then the winning number is drawn [[after]] all [[bet]]s are submitted}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|maghuweteng|anak ng huweteng}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|tambiyolo}}
* {{l|tl|wahoy}}

