Page 7047 Indio: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|Indiyo|indiyo}}
* {{alt|tl|Indyo|indyo}}

===Etymology===
{{ubor|tl|es|indio|t=[[native]] of the {{w|Spanish East Indies}}, especially the {{w|Captaincy General of the Philippines}}}}. The term in {{ncog|es|-}} itself was originally [[neutral]] in [[connotation]], just like how it is perceived with [[Native American]]s in {{w|Latin America}} and [[Indian]]s from [[India]], called in the same way in Spanish. It later became understood as a [[derogatory]] term in the Philippines in the later years of the {{w|History of the Philippines (1565–1898)|Spanish colonial period}}, especially during the {{w|Philippine Revolution}}, likely due to some historical [[condescending]] usage. See {{m|tl|indoy|t=ugly}}. See also {{ncog|id|inlander}}, {{ncog|ceb|inday}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|Indi.ó|IPA2=Índi.o}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|Indió|head2=Índió|b=Indiyo}}

# {{lb|tl|historical|derogatory}} [[native]] of the [[Philippines]] {{gl|during the Spanish colonial period in the Philippines}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|indoy}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|Sangley}} / {{l|tl|Tsino}}
* {{l|tl|mestiso}} / {{l|tl|mestisa}}
* {{l|tl|insulares}}
* {{l|tl|peninsulares}}
* {{l|tl|Kastila}} / {{l|tl|Espanyol}}
* {{l|tl|Amerikano}}
* {{l|tl|Filipino}}
* {{l|tl|Negrito}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:KWF Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* [https://www.tagaloglang.com/indio/ “INDIO” in ''Tagalog-English Dictionary'', TAGALOG LANG, 2007.]
* [https://www.tagaloglang.com/indiyo/ “INDIYO” in ''Tagalog-English Dictionary'', TAGALOG LANG, 2007.]
* {{R:tl:Hispanismos 1972|page=336|q=indiyó}}
-------- end text --------
