* {{alt|tl|inet||colloquial}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*qinit||heat of the sun; hot}} (cf. {{cog|bcl|init}}, {{cog|ceb|init}}, {{cog|cyo|init}}, {{cog|hil|init}}, {{cog|msk|init||sweat}}), from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*qinit}} (cf. {{cog|txe|init||sweat}}, {{cog|pmf|ini||sweat}}, {{cog|wlo|ini||sweat}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|i|nit}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[heat]]; [[hotness]]
#: {{syn|tl|kainitan}}
#: {{ux|tl|Natuyo sa '''init''' ng apoy ang mga basa kong kamay.|My wet hands got dry from the '''heat''' of the fire.}}
# [[warmth]]; [[sultriness]] {{gl|of weather}}
#: {{syn|tl|banas|alisis|alinsangan}}
# [[temperature]]
#: {{syn|tl|temperatura|kaintan}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[ardor]]; [[fervor]]; [[excitement]]
#: {{syn|tl|sigla|kasiglahan}}
# {{lb|tl|figurative}} [[ire]]; [[anger]]; [[wrath]]
#: {{syn|tl|galit|ngitngit|poot}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} [[sexual]] [[desire]]
#: {{syn|tl|libog|kalibugan}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} [[rut]]; [[estrus]] {{gl|in animals}}
#: {{syn|tl|kandi|pangangandi|landi|paglalandi}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kainitan|magpainit|painitin|magkainitan|magpainit|mainit|initin|initan|mainit ang ulo|mapag-initan|napakainit|pampainit|tag-init|uminit|walang-init|init ng ulo|uminit ang ulo|kaintan|initbiling|initbulog|initbutod|initdagitban|initdanumsigwasan|initkapnayan|initsigan|initsipat|initsukat|initsukatan|initsupil|pag-initan|papag-initin|sala sa init, sala sa lamig|jinet|mainit sa kamay|mainit sa mata}}

