Page 7514 j: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor-lite|tl|es|j}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der-lite|tl|en|j}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der-lite|tl|es|j}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyph-lite|tl|j}} <!-- {{hyph|tl|j}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Filipino alphabet}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/djej/|[d͡ʒɛɪ̯]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|dyey}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Abecedario}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/ˈhota/|[ˈho.tɐ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|hota}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/dj/|[d͡ʒ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|j}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme|Spanish unadapted loanwords}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/h/|[h]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|h}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme|Spanish unadapted loanwords|obsolete}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/s/|[s]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|s}} -->
* {{rhymes-lite|tl|ej|ota|s1=1|s2=2}}

===Letter===
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|J|Baybayin spelling|ᜇ᜔ᜌᜒᜌ᜔|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|10|dyey|alphabet name={{w|Filipino alphabet}}}}

====Usage notes====
* This letter is mostly used only in slang, proper nouns, or unadapted loanwords.
* Some purists of Tagalog replace ''j'' in words with ''dy''.

====See also====
* {{list:Latin script letters/tl}}

===Letter===
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|J|Baybayin spelling|ᜑᜓᜆ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|11|jota|alphabet name={{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}}}

====Usage notes====
* Some Spanish words originally with Spanish ''j'' tend to be replaced with ''h'' in Tagalog.

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

-------- end text --------
