Page 7596 k: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor-lite|tl|es|k}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der-lite|tl|en|k}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by Baybayin character {{m-lite|tl|ᜃ|sc=Tglg|tr=ka}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der-lite|tl|es|k}}.

The use of {{angbr|k}} instead of using the Spanish-based {{angbr|c}} and {{angbr|q}} was promoted in the late 19th century primarily by the educated (such as {{w|José Rizal}} and {{w|Trinidad Pardo de Tavera}}) because of the Baybayin character primarily being applicable to all vowels, as well as the ease of usage with Tagalog grammar rules. Its order in the Abakada alphabet was due to the order of the similar sounding {{angbr|c}} in the Spanish alphabet.

====Pronunciation====
* {{hyph-lite|tl|k}} <!-- {{hyph|tl|k}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Filipino alphabet}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/kej/|[kɛɪ̯]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|key}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Abakada alphabet|Abecedario}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/ka/|[kɐ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|ka}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/k/|[k]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme|intervocalic}} {{IPA-lite|tl|/k/|[x]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA}} -->
* {{rhymes-lite|tl|ej|a|s=1}}

====Letter====
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|K|Baybayin spelling|ᜃᜒᜌ᜔|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|11|key|alphabet name={{w|Filipino alphabet}}}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letters/tl}}

====Letter====
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|K|Baybayin spelling|ᜃ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|3|ka|alphabet name={{w|Abakada alphabet}}}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|12|ka|alphabet name={{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA|key}}

====Interjection====
{{tl-head|interjection|b=key}}

# {{lb|tl|Internet slang|text messaging}} [[OK]]

