Page 7600 ka-: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{rfe|tl}}

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# {{n-g|implies companionship or partnership when prefixed to a root}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|sama|kasama|gloss1=to accompany|gloss2=partner}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|opisina|kaopisina|gloss1=office|gloss2=coworker}}
# {{n-g|implies similarity or interaction when prefixed to a root noun}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|mukha|kamukha|gloss1=face|gloss2=someone/something similar; look-alike}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|away|kaaway|gloss1=fight|gloss2=enemy}}
# {{n-g|implies repeated action when prefixed to a root that repeats the first syllable}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|sigaw|kasisigaw|gloss1=shout|gloss2=repeatedly shouting}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|isip|kaiisip|gloss1=mind, thought|gloss2=thinking a lot}}
# {{n-g|implies causing or producing something in an extreme degree when prefixed to a root that repeats the first two syllables}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|galang|kagalang-galang|gloss1=respect|gloss2=inspiring great respect}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|paniwala|kapani-paniwala|gloss1=belief|gloss2=very plausible}}
# {{n-g|implies recent action when prefixed to a root that repeats the first syllable and followed by {{m|tg|lang}} or {{m|tg|lamang}}}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|punta|kapupunta|gloss1=going|gloss2=recently went}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|luto|kaluluto|gloss1=cooking, cuisine|gloss2=recently cooked}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}

===See also===
* {{l|tl|kaka-}}

-------- end text --------
Page 7601 ka- -an: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|ca- -an||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|ka- -han}}
* {{alt|tl|ka- -nan}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|map-pro|*ka- -an}} (compare {{cog|ms|ke- -an}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|ka- -an}}

===Circumfix===
{{tl-head|circumfix|b=+|b2=ka- an}}

# {{ngd|used to form abstract nouns}}
#: {{afex|tl|payapa|t1=peaceful|ka- -an|kapayapaan|t3=peace}}
#: {{afex|tl|malay|t1=awareness|ka- -an|kamalayan|t3=consciousness}}
# {{ngd|used to form nouns indicating a larger location}}
#: {{afex|tl|gubat|t1=woods|ka- -an|kagubatan|t3=forest}}
#: {{afex|tl|dagat|t1=sea|ka- -an|karagatan|t3=ocean}}
# {{ngd|used to form proper nouns indicating a domain of a people or place}}
#: {{afex|tl|Tagalog|t1=Tagalog|ka- -an|Katagalugan|t3=Tagalog area}}
#: {{afex|tl|Bisaya|t1=Visayan|ka- -an|Kabisayaan|t3=Visayas; Visayan area}}
#: {{afex|tl|Maynila|t1=Manila|ka- -an|Kamaynilaan|t3=Metro Manila; Manila area}}
# {{ngd|used to form words meaning “one who receives or  ({{m|tl|-an}}) from someone ({{m|tl|ka-}})”}}
#: {{afex|tl|ibig|t1=love|ka- -an|kaibigan|t3=friend; person who receives love from someone; lover}}
#: {{afex|tl|halik|t1=kiss|ka- -an|kahalikan|t3=person who receives kisses from someone; kissing-mate}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally, {{IPAchar|/h/}} is inserted before ''-an'' when the root word ends with a vowel that is not followed by a glottal stop. In some cases, phoneme change can occur and {{IPAchar|/h/}} becomes {{IPAchar|/n/}}.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|saya|[[kasiyahan|kasiya'''h'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|dami|[[karamihan|karami'''h'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|gusto|[[kagustuhan|kagustu'''h'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|bihasa|[[kabihasnan|kabihas'''n'''an]]}}
* Due to [[allophony]], {{IPAchar|/d/}} turns into {{IPAchar|/r/}} when inserted before ''-an'' or after ''ka-''.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|baliktad|[[kabaligtaran|kabalikta'''r'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|lunod|[[kanluran|kanlu'''r'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|gawad|[[kagawaran|kagawa'''r'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|dami|[[karamihan|ka'''r'''amihan]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|dangal|[[karangalan|ka'''r'''angalan]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|danas|[[karanasan|ka'''r'''anasan]]}}
* Sense 4: The ''ka-'' prefix has a stress while the stress of the root shifts syllables to the right. For roots with stress on the last syllable, the stress goes to ''-an''.

====Derived terms====
{{circumfixsee|tl}}
-------- end text --------
