Page 7918 kalapati: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|calapati||obsolete|Abecedario}}
* {{alt|tl|palapati||obsolete}}
* {{alt|tl|palipati||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Supposedly {{m|tl|palapati}}, {{bor+|tl|ms|parapati|nocap=1||pigeon}}, from {{der|tl|sa|पारापत||pigeon}}. According to Potet (2016), the word was borrowed via written Malay. The Jawi {{m|ms|ڤ|tr=p}} was misread as {{m|ms|ق|tr=q}}. Thus, changing the {{IPAchar|/p/}} into a {{IPAchar|/k/}} when spoken. Compare {{cog|pag|malapati}}, {{cog|pam|patipati}}, {{cog|bcl|salampati}}, {{cog|ceb|pati}}, {{cog|mrw|marampatik}}, {{cog|tsg|māpati}}, and {{cog|ms|merpati}}. {{doublet|tl|patipati}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|tl|ati|s=4}}
* {{hyph|tl|ka|la|pa|ti}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|ornithology}} [[dove]]; [[pigeon]]
#: {{syn|tl|paloma|patipati}}
# {{lb|tl|euphemism}} [[prostitute]]
#: {{syn|tl|puta|pokpok}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kalapating mababa ang lipad|kalapating-gubat|kalapatihan|mangalapati|pangangalapati|magkakalapati|taeng kalapati|kalapating ligaw|kalapating manso|kalapating sugo|magkalapati|bahay-kalapati|maamong kalapati|mag-asawang kalapati}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|balud|pitson|batubato|lanatan|siyete kolores|punay|punyalada|kurukutok|bambanin|batubatong-sili|batubatong-katigbi|agbaan|batik-lawin|batubatong-dinampol|lapati}}

