Page 8648 kawani: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|cauani||obsolete|Abecedario}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|tl|ka|wani}}, according to Panganiban (1972).

Alternatively, {{bor+|tl|ms|kerani||clerk|nocap=1}} (written in Jawi as {{m|ms|کراني}}), ultimately from {{der|tl|ta|கிராணி||clerk}} or from {{der|tl|sa|करण|t=scribe}}. Theories on the linkage from Malay include:

* According to Potet (2016), when the word was introduced to Tagalog, the Jawi letter {{m|ms|ر|tr=r}} was probably mistaken for the letter {{m|ms|و|tr=w}}.
* According to Zorc (1981), the {{IPAchar|/r/}} possibly shifted to {{IPAchar|/l/}} when borrowed then the {{IPAchar|/l/}} was lost later on and became {{IPAchar|/w/}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|kawaní}}
{{tl-IPA}} {{q|nonstandard}}
* {{hyph|tl|ka|wa|ni}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|kawaní|head2=+|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|formal}} [[employee]]
#: {{syn|tl|empleado|tauhan}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''kawani''' ng pamahalaan|government '''employee'''}}
# [[helper]]; [[aid]]; [[assistant]]
#: {{syn|tl|katulong|katulungin}}

====Derived terms====
{{col3|tl|kawanihan|Kawanihan ng Adwana}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|eskribyente}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|awaní|head2=+|b=+}}

# [[working]] as an [[employee]] or [[helper]]

