===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA|kawî}}
* {{hyph|tl|ka|wi}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|kawî|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|obsolete}}

# [[reveal]]ing of an [[accomplice]] more than what is necessary

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|kumawi|magkawi|mangkawi|kawiin|makawi}}

===Etymology 2===
Possibly from {{der|tl|jv|ꦏꦮꦶ|tr={{l|jv|kawi}}|t=poet}}, from {{der|tl|kaw|kawi|t=poet}}, from {{der|tl|sa|कवि||poet}}. Compare {{cog|id|kawi}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA|kawì}}
* {{hyph|tl|ka|wi}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|kawì|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|linguistics|obsolete}}

# [[jargon]] {{gl|for two people especially when they do not want to be understood by others}}
#: {{syn|tl|balbal|islang|[[salita]]ng [[malabo]]|takitaki|tigbuhol}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Kawian''' mo siyang pakiusapan.|Talk to him '''using jargons'''.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Fr. Domingo de los Santos (1835) gave several examples of '''kawi''' in usage, such as ''gonco'' for {{m|tl|kugon}}, ''sapu'' for {{m|tl|pusa}}, ''soa'' for {{m|tl|aso}}, ''bigtu'' for {{m|tl|tubig}}, ''saang drengpacotaba'' for {{m|tl|ang}} {{m|tl|sa}} {{m|tl|padre|padreng}} {{m|tl|tabako}}, ''golin'' for {{m|tl|Linggo}}, ''drope'' for {{m|tl|Pedro}}, and ''onng̃aylis na'' for {{m|tl|ngayon}} {{m|tl|nalis}} (past tense of {{m|tl|malis}}, archaic alternative form of {{m|tl|umalis}}).

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|magkawi|kawiin|ikawi|kawian}}

=====See also=====
{{col3|tl|bangkiwi}}

