Page 8890 kiyaw-kiyaw: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|kiyawkiyaw}}
* {{alt|tl|kyaw-kyaw|kyawkyaw}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|tl|nan-hbl|-}}, according to English (1987) and Panganiban (1972). According to Chan-Yap (1980), it comes from {{ncog|nan-hbl|-}} {{m-g|''kiaù-kiaù''}}, which she defines as {{m-g|incessant}}, as in {{m-g|''kiaù+kiaù+k<sup>h</sup>aǔ''}} with the latter verb she mentions as {{ncog|nan-hbl|哭|tr=khàu}}. The {{m-g|''kiaù-kiaù''}} she refers to may possibly be {{ncog|nan-hbl|攪攪|tr=kiáu-kiáu}} or {{m|nan-hbl|噭噭|tr=kiàu-kiàu}} as found in Ogawa (1932). Compare {{cog|ceb|kyawkyaw}} and {{ncog|nan-hbl|噭噭叫|tr=kiàu-kiàu-kiò|t=with all voices in a jumble}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|kiyáw-kiyáw}}
* {{hyph|tl|ki|yaw-ki|yaw}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|kiyáw-kiyáw|b=+}}

# [[nonsensical]] [[complaint]]s or [[moaning]]s; [[useless]] [[fretting]] or [[worry]]; [[incessant]] [[nagging]]; [[rumbling]]; [[flurry]]
#: {{syn|tl|kiyaw|kuskós-balungos}}
# [[unnecessary]] [[detail]]s or [[action]] that slows down the work
#: {{syn|tl|kuntil-butil}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|makiyaw-kiyaw}}

