Page 8896 KKK: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|K.K.K.}}

[[Image:Philippine revolution flag kkk1.svg|thumb|Unang watawat ng mga Katipunan na nagpapakita ng "'''KKK'''" (The first flag of the Katipunan showing the abbreviation "'''KKK'''")]]

===Etymology===
{{initialism|tl|[[kataas-taasan|Kataas-taasan]]g [[kagalang-galang]]ang [[Katipunan]] [[ng]] [[mga]] [[Anak ng Bayan]]|t=Highest, Most Respected Assembly of the Children/Sons of the Nation}}, the full name of the [[Katipunan]].

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|key key key}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun}}

# {{abbr of|tl|Katipunan}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1968|author=Jean Donald Bowen|title=Babasahing Panggitnang Baytang Sa Tagalog|publisher=Univ of California Press|page=153
|passage=[...Basahin kung ano pa ang ibang nangyari sa Katipunan.] Ang “Kataas-taasan,  Kagalang-galangang Katipunan ng mga Anak ng Bayan&quot; o ang “'''K.K.K.'''“ na lalong kilala sa tawag na Katipunan, ay isang samahang lihim ng mga  manghihimagsik&nbsp;...
|translation=[...Read what more happened to the Katipunan.] The “Kataas-taasan,  Kagalang-galangang Katipunan ng mga Anak ng Bayan&quot; or the “'''K.K.K.'''“ more especially known as Katipunan, is a secret organization of revolutionaries&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1975|title=General [quezon] Education Journal
|passage=Ibig sabihin nito&#39;y hindi na kinikilala ng pamahalaan ang '''KKK''', bagamat ang pag-iral ng mga lokal na sangay ay hindi kaagad nagwakas.
|translation=This means the government no longer recognizes the '''KKK''', although the implementation of local branches did not end immediately.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1992|author=Santiago V. Alvarez|title=The Katipunan and the Revolution: Memoirs of a General : with the Original Tagalog Text|publisher=Ateneo University Press|isbn=9789715500777
|passage=Napag-usapan ang pagbabangon ng isang Alituntuning-Batas (Constitucion),  bagaman mayroon na ang '''K.K.K.''', na siyang pinagbabatayan ng mga  Pamunuang Sanggunian at Balangay; mga kaugaliang sinusunod.
|t=The establishment of a Rule of Law (Constitution) was discussed, although the K.K.K. already has one, which is being used as the basis of the Leadership Councils and the Members; customs that are followed.}}
-------- end text --------
