Page 9368 kumukulo ang dugo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|blood is boiling}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|kumukulô ang dugô}}
* {{hyph|tl|ku|mu|ku|lo ang du|go}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|[[kumukulô]] [[ang]] [[dugô]]|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|idiomatic}} [[blood-boiling]]; [[furious]]; [[angry]]
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1994|author=Leonardo N. Mercado|title=The Filipino Mind|publisher=CRVP|isbn=9781565180635|page=30
|passage=... for an intractable person Hirap ng kalooban Pasakit Pain Iniingatan sa loob  Iniipon sa dibdib Feeling kept secret Isama ng loob Ikakulo ng dugo Anger Kaba ng loob Takot, nerbiyos Fear, nervousness Kahinaan ng loob Kahinaan ng tuhod  Fear Kalamayin ang loob Pahupain ang galit To reduce anger or o matinding lungkot sadness Kalinasan ng loob Di-pagtatanaw-tama, Not to be in agreement pagkakasalisi ng damdamin Kumukulo ang loob '''Kumukulo ang dugo''', Very  angry galit&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1999|author=Gary B. Palmer; Debra J. Occhi|title=Languages of Sentiment: Cultural Constructions of Emotional Substrates|publisher=John Benjamins Publishing|isbn=9789027251381|page=194
|passage=... HAVING THICK SKIN balat-karabaw &#39;skin-carabao (thick skinned, no shame)&#39;  balat-sibuyas &#39;skin-onion (thin skinned, sensitive)&#39; makapal ang mukha &#39;thick face  (impenetrable, no shame)&#39; THE BODY IS A CONTAINER FOR FEARLESSNESS/ BRAVERY malakas and loob &#39;inside swells (fearless)&#39; THE BODY IS A  CONTAINER FOR GRIEF parang puputok ang dibdib like a bursting chest ( extreme grief or sorrow)&#39; THE BODY IS A CONTAINER FOR ANGER '''kumukulo ang dugo''' &#39;blood&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2012|author=A. Gülerce|title=Re(con)figuring Psychoanalysis: Critical Juxtapositions of the Philosophical, the Sociohistorical and the Political|publisher=Springer|isbn=9780230373303
|passage=... withemotions invoked in Filipino metaphors '''Kumukulo ang dugo''' ko (My blood is  boiling)and Natutuyo ang dugo ko (My blood is drying up or drained). Folk  physiology and anatomy figured crucially in the traditional Filipino worldview  which resonated with.}}
-------- end text --------
