Page 9412 kunwari: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|conouari|conovari|conuari||obsolete|Abecedario}}
* {{alt|tl|kunowari|kunuwari}}
* {{alt|tl|kunwa|kunowa|kunuwa}}
* {{alt|tl|kunware||colloquial}}
* {{alt|tl|kunyari|kungyari}}
* {{alt|tl|kunya}}
* {{alt|tl|kunyare||colloquial}}

===Etymology===
Commonly believed to be from {{univerbation|tl|kung|wari|nocap=1|t1=if|t2=deliberation}}. However, according to the Vocabulario de lengua tagala (1613), the word is from {{univ|tl|kuno|t1=alleging|wari|t2=seemingly|nocap=1}} and therefore could be a {{sync|tl|nocap=1}} of earlier variant {{m|tl|kunuwari}}. Compare {{cog|pag|kunwari}} and {{cog|pam|kanuari}}, {{m|pam|kunuari}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|kunwarì}}
{{tl-IPA|kunwarè}} {{q|colloquial}}
* {{hyph|tl|kun|wa|ri}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|kunwarì|b=+}}

# [[simulated]]; [[pretend]]; [[feigned]]; [[make believe]]; [[false]]; [[fictitious]]
#: {{syn|tl|nagkukunwari|[[hindi]] [[totoo]]}}

===Adverb===
{{tl-adv|kunwarì|b=+}}

# [[as if]]; [[pretendingly]]; in a [[make believe]] [[way]]
# [[for instance]]; [[for example]]; [[as if]]; [[like]]
#: {{syn|tl|halimbawa|kumbaga|parang}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|kunwarì|b=+}}

# [[feigning]]; [[simulation]]; [[pretense]]; [[bluff]]
#: {{syn|tl|panggap|pagkukunwa|pagdadahilan|pagpapanggap}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|magkunwari|mapagkunwari|nagkukunwari|pakunwari|pagkukunwari|pagpapakunwari|magpakunwari|makipagkunwari|pakikipagkunwarian|pagkunwarian|kunwa-kunwarian|pakikipagkunwari|kunwarian|tagakunwari|pangkunwari|pagkakakunwari|napakakunwari|pagkakunwari|makakunwari}}

