===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|nan-hbl|-}} {{zh-l|龜公|tr=kui-kong|t=pimp; brothelkeeper}}, according to Manuel (1948). Alternatively, according to Chan-Yap (1980), it is from {{zh-l|雞公|tr=koe-kong|t=rooster; cock}}, but the pronunciation "''koe-kong''" is not used in relevant Hokkien dialects and does not mean "rooster", while the relevant pronunciations "''koe-kang''" and "''ke-kang''" are more phonologically distant from the word ''kuwekong''.

