===Etymology===
{{glossary|Borrowed}} from [[w:Philippine Spanish|Philippine]] {{bor|tl|es|lanzón|lanzones, lanzón|[[lanzon]]}}, from {{der|tl|ms|langsat}}. The spelling was patterned after {{cog|es|lanzones}}, plural of {{cog|es|lanzón||short, thick spear}}, possibly because the borrowed term from Malay was heard as a variant of {{cog|es|lanza||lance}} and the leaves of the tree somehow resemble a lance. Compare {{cog|th|ลางสาด}}, {{cog|jv|ꦭꦁꦱꦼꦧ꧀}}, and {{cog|cmn|榔色|tr=láng sè}} and {{cog|nan-hbl|蘭撒|tr=lân-sat}}.

