{{bor+|tl|nan-hbl|落落|tr=làu-làu|t=loose}}, according to Manuel (1948),<ref>{{R:tl:Manuel 1948|q=lawláw|page=35}}</ref> or possibly a {{glossary|reduplication}} of {{cog|nan-hbl|老|tr=lāu|t=old}} according to Chan-Yap (1980).<ref>{{R:tl:Chan-Yap 1980|page=130}}</ref> However, Zorc (1985) disagrees and offers a more native etymon.<ref>{{R:CEDOF|4|209}}</ref> Compare {{cog|ceb|lawlaw}} and {{cog|pam|lolo}}.

