Page 10104 laya: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Possibly from a {{blend|tl|layaw|haya|t1=satisfaction of one's needs and desires|t2=at ease; allow; tolerate|nocap=1}}, according to {{w|Virgilio S. Almario}} (1992). However, historian {{w|Zeus A. Salazar}} (1999) argued that the word was a standalone word and was already part of the Tagalog vocabulary by mid-19th century despite not being included in Fr. Noceda and Sanlucar's ''{{w|Vocabulario de la lengua tagala}}''. In addition, {{m|tl|malaya||free}} was listed as a surname in the ''{{w|Catálogo alfabético de apellidos}}'' which was first published 1849.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|layà,+<q:obsolete><n^>|layâ<a^>|new=1}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|layà|b=+}}

