===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*lima}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*lima}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*lima}}. Compare {{cog|tay|zima'}}, {{cog|xnb|rima}}, {{cog|mad|lema}}, {{cog|mg|dimy}}, {{cog|mi|rima}}, {{cog|min|limo}}, {{cog|rap|rima}}, and {{cog|ssf|rima}}, {{cog|tiy|limo}}, {{cog|to|nima}}, and {{cog|urk|ลีมา|tr=lima}}. See also {{noncog|sa|नेम||half}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|limá}}
* {{hyph|tl|li|ma}}
* {{audio|tl|TL-PH-lima.ogg|Audio}}

===Numeral===
{{tl-num|limá|b=+}}

# [[five]]
#: {{syn|tl|singko}}

====Usage notes====
* To describe the quantity of something, the number is placed before the noun and affixed with a '''-ng''' when the word ends with a vowel, and a separate word {{m|tl|na}} for a consonant.
*: {{ux|tl|'''Isang''' saging, '''dalawang''' pinya.|One banana, two pineapples.}}
*: {{ux|tl|'''Apat na''' mansanas, '''anim na''' mangga.|Four apples, six mangoes.}}

