{{tl-noun|máginoó|b=+}}

# [[gentleman]]
#: {{syn|tl|ginoo}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} the [[ruling class]] or [[nobility]] in ancient Tagalog society

====Usage notes====
* According to Fr. Juan de Noceda and Fr. Pedro del San Lucar who compiled the ''Vocabulario de la lengua tagala'' in 1754, '''''maginoo''''' referred to a ''gentleman of rank'' while {{m|tl|ginoo}} referred to a ''lady of rank'', whereas today, both refer to men.

