Page 11626 maharlika: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|Maharlika}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|mahadlica|mahad-lica|mahaglica||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}
* {{alt|tl|mahadlika|mahaglika||obsolete}}
* {{alt|tl|maharlica||archaic}}

===Etymology===
From a {{metathesis|tl|}} of {{der|tl|sa|महर्द्धिक||[[prosperous]]}}. Compare {{cog|pam|mardika}}, {{cog|mrw|maradika'}} / {{m|mrw|mirdika}}, {{cog|tsg|mahardikaꞌ}}, {{cog|bug|ᨆᨑᨉᨙᨀ|tr={{l|bug|maradeka}}}}, {{cog|jv|ꦩꦂꦢꦶꦏ}}, {{cog|ban|ᬫᬃᬤᬾᬓ|tr=mardéka}}, {{cog|id|mahardika}}, and {{cog|ms|merdeka}}. The gay slang sense is due to the similarity with the word {{m|tl|mahal}}, which also came from {{der|tl|sa|-}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|maharliká}}
{{tl-IPA|maharlikâ}}
{{tl-IPA|mahárlika}} {{q|colloquial}}
* {{hyph|tl|ma|har|li|ka}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|maharliká|head2=maharlikâ|head3=mahárliká|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|historical}} [[freeman]]; a member of the [[feudal]] [[warrior]] class in ancient [[Tagalog]] [[society]]
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} act of [[free]]ing someone
#: {{syn|tl|laya}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|kamaharlikaan|magmaharlika|maharlikain|pagkamaharlika|pagmaharlika|Maharnilad}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|mahal|maharaha|maharani}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|timawa}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|maharliká|head2=maharlikâ|head3=mahárliká|b=+}}

# [[noble#Adjective|noble]]; [[aristocratic]]
#: {{syn|tl|dakila|noblesa|kagalang-galang|kamahalan|dugong bughaw}}
# {{lb|tl|gay slang}} [[expensive]]
#: {{syn|tl|mahal|Mahalia Jackson|q2=gay slang}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[free]] {{gl|from slavery}}
#: {{syn|tl|malaya}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[plebeian]]; [[common]]
#: {{syn|tl|karaniwan}}

====Usage notes====
* The word '''''maharlika''''' used to refer to the [[middle class]] of ancient Tagalog society. During the {{w|History of the_Philippines (1965–1986)|Kilusang Bagong Lipunan}} era in the Philippines, former President {{w|Ferdinand Marcos Sr.}} claimed that ''maharlika'' referred to the nobility of ancient Tagalog society. Because of this, ''maharlika'' evolved into modern use to mean “nobility” but the correct terminology for it was the {{m|tl|maginoo}} class.

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|hadlika}}

===References===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=289}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1613|389|Libre) Maharlica (pp) de eſclauonia}}

{{C|tl|Nobility|Slavery}}
