{{bor+|tl|es|macan|t=bruised}}, an [[inflection]] of {{m|es|macar|t=to bruise}}, although according to Manuel (1948), it is supposedly from {{m|tl|Macao}}, due to Noceda & Sanlucar (1860) defining it as ''"Arroz de tubigan, bueno y oloroso, uno es blanco y otro colorado. Vino la semilla de Macan."'' and an early account of Fr. {{w|Domingo de Salazar}} (1583) saying that they have located it at ''"la ysla de Macan, donde viven los Portugueses que estan junto a la ciudad de Cantón, en la China,..."''.

