Page 12080 mami: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=tl}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|bami}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|tl|nan-hbl|-}}, either:
* {{m|nan-hbl|肉麵|tr=mah-mī|t=meat and noodles soup|lit=meat and noodles}}, according to Chan-Yap (1980). Compare {{cog|ceb|bam-i}}, {{cog|id|bakmi}}, {{cog|jv|ꦧꦏ꧀ꦩꦶ}}, {{cog|nl|bami}}. See also {{noncog|nan-hbl|牛肉麵|tr=gû-mah-mī|t=beef noodles}}.
* {{m|nan-hbl|[[馬]][[麵]]|tr=má mī|lit=Ma’s noodles}}, noodles peddled by {{w|Ma Mon Luk}} (<span class="Hans">馬文祿</span> ／ <span class="Hans">马文禄</span>, {{nowrap|{{w|Cantonese Yale}}: ''Máh Màhn-luhk''}}; {{nowrap|{{w|Pe̍h-ōe-jī}}: ''Má Bûn Lo̍k''}}) in his restaurant since the 1920s in [[Binondo]], [[Manila]].
Manuel (1948) also records an entry, providing the definitions and pronunciation of {{ncog|nan-hbl|肉麵|tr=mah-mī|t=meat and noodles soup|lit=meat and noodles}}, but misidentifies it as {{ncog|yue|-}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|ma|mi}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{l|en|mami}} {{gl|a [[soup]] [[dish]] of [[wheat]] [[noodles]] or [[cellophane noodles]] mixed with various [[meat]] and [[vegetables]]}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|bami|pansit mami|tsami|lomi}}

