Page 12171 mandin: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{compound|tl|man|din}}. The ancient compound ''mandin'' cannot be separated. Compare {{m|tl|naman}} and {{m|tl|man lamang}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|mandín}}

===Adverb===
{{tl-adv|mandín|b=+}}

# [[unexpectedly]]; [[suddenly]]
#: {{syn|tl|agad|kaagad}}
#: {{ux|tl|Nang magkita kami, '''mandin''' ay tumayo siya't nakipagbatian sa akin.|When we met, she '''suddenly''' stood up and greeted with me.}}
# it [[seem]]s; [[perhaps]]; [[apparently]]
#: {{syn|tl|wari|tila|marahil}}
# [[nevertheless]]; [[yet]]
#: {{syn|tl|gayumpaman}}
# {{lb|tl|now|_|chiefly|_|Marinduque|Mindoro|Rizal|uncommon|_|in|_|Bulacan}} [[definitely]]; [[indeed]]; [[without doubt]]
#: {{syn|tl|ngani}}
#: {{ux|tl|Namamatay '''mandin'''.|It's '''definitely''' dying.}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Mandin''' [[pa]]!|'''Indeed'''!}}
# {{lb|tl|Marinduque}} [[isn't it]]? [[right]]?
#: {{ux|tl|Mahal mo '''mandin''' ako?|'''Don't''' you love me?}}

====Usage notes====
* Can be made the first word (predicate) or an enclitic particle.
* Fairly rare in contemporary [[Manileño]] Tagalog, which is Standard Tagalog.

====See also====
{{col3|tl|talaga}}

===References===
* {{R:KWF Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Pinoy Dictionary}}
