Page 12529 Marikina: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|Mariquina||archaic}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|tl}}, but certain etymologies exist:

* ''Marikina'' is named after a young priest named ''Mariquina''.
* Pre-Hispanic oral tradition says that ''Marikina'' is named after a lady named ''Maria Cuina''.
* ''Marikina'' is intended to be the name of a chapel, born out from linguistic misunderstanding, and derived from "{{m|tl|marikit}} ''na po''", said of a Filipino worker.
* ''Marikina'' is named after the town of {{w|Mariquina}} in Spain.
* Based on historical documents held by the Marikina city government, ''Marikina'' is originally called ''Mariquit-na'' (''Marikit-na'') before it is renamed after {{w|Félix Berenguer de Marquina}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|Ma|ri|ki|na}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=+}}

# {{place|tl|city|t=Marikina|region/Metro Manila|c/Philippines}}
# {{place|tl|t=Marikina|river|c/Philippines}}
-------- end text --------
