{{bor+|tl|es|Mendiola}}, from {{der|tl|eu|Mendiola|lit=mountain hut}}. The street is named after Enrique Mendiola, an educator, textbook author, and member of the first Board of Regents of the University of the Philippines.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|Men|di|o|la}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=mendiyola}}

# {{surname|tl|from=Spanish < Basque}}
# {{w|Mendiola Street}}, a [[street]] in [[Manila]] and frequently been the site of often violent confrontations between protesters and government troops protecting {{w|Malacañang Palace}}

====Statistics====
* {{surname-philippines-forebears|name=Mendiola|rank=202nd|count=33,963}}

