Page 13001 mga: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|mañga|mang̃a|man͠ga|m̃ga|mg̃a|m͠ga||obsolete|Abecedario}}
* {{alt|tl|manga||archaic}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|tl|manga}}, from Proto-Central Philippine ''*maŋa'', from {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*maŋa}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*maŋa}}.

The three-letter spelling originated in a now defunct Spanish language abbreviation convention of drawing a tilde over the abbreviated word, in this case {{m|tl|manga}}, later rendered as {{m|tl|mg̃a}} or {{m|tl|m͠ga}}. The complications of typing {{angbr|ñ}}, {{angbr|g̃}} or any such tilded combination using English language typewriters during the American occupation of the Philippines caused it to be dropped in writing. Compare {{m|tl|ng}}.

The abbreviated form was kept to avoid possible confusion with prefix {{m|tl|manga-}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{audio|tl|Tl-ph-mga.ogg|Audio}}

===Particle===
{{tl-head|particle|b=+}}

# {{n-g|used to pluralize nouns}}: [[-s]], [[-es]]
#: {{uxi|tl|'''mga''' aso|dog'''s'''}}

===Adverb===
{{tl-adv|b=+}}

# [[approximately]]; [[around]]; [[about]]
#: {{syn|tl|halos|humigit-kumulang|banda|q3=place, time}}
#: {{ux|tl|Alis tayo '''mga''' alas tres ng hapon.|Let's leave '''around''' 3 pm.}}
#: {{ux|tl|Siguro '''mga''' sampung piso lang iyong pamasahe.|Maybe the fare is '''around''' ₱10.}}

===Further reading===
