Page 13053 Mindoro: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Usually attributed by folk etymologies to {{ncog|es|[[mina de oro]]||[[gold mine]]}}. However, there is little evidence of gold mining activities on the island. Furthermore, old Tagalog documents name the island ''Minolo''. ''Minolo'' may be related to ''minuro'', an old Visayan term meaning "place of abundance", from ''duro'', "abundance".

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|Min|do|ro}}

===Proper noun===
