Page 13432 -nan: -------- begin text --------

===Suffix===
{{tl-verb|b=+|addlpos=noun,adverb}}

# {{alt form of|tl|-an|nocap=1|nodot=1}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|talo|t1=defeat|talunan|t2=loser}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|tawa|t1=laugh|tawanan|t2=laughter; to laugh}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|sapupo|t1=the act of sitting on the lap|sinapupunan|t2=lap}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|kuha|t1=take|kunan|t2=to take a picture or video}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally, {{IPAchar|/h/}} is inserted before {{m|tl|-an}} when the root word ends with a vowel that is not followed by a glottal stop. In some cases, phoneme change can occur and {{IPAchar|/h/}} becomes {{IPAchar|/n/}}.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|talo|[[talunan|talu'''n'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|tawa|[[tawanan|tawa'''n'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sapupo|[[sinapupunan|sinapupu'''n'''an]]}}
* Sometimes, the final vowel of the root word disappears when the suffix is added.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|kuha|kunan}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|tl}}
* {{l|tl|ka- -nan}}
