Page 13443 nang: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|tl|aŋ|s=1}}

===Conjunction===
{{tl-head|conjunction|b=+}}

# [[when]], at the time of ({{n-g|referring to past events}})
#: {{syn|tl|noong}}
#: {{ux|tl|Natutulog na ang mga bata '''nang''' dumating kami.|The children were already sleeping '''when''' we came.}}
# [[for]], [[so that]], [[in order to]]
#: {{syn|tl|para|upang}}
#: {{ux|tl|Bilisan mo '''nang''' makahabol ka pa!|Hurry '''so that''' you can still catch up!}}

===Particle===
{{tl-head|particle|b=+}}

# {{n-g|combination of {{m|tl|na}} and {{m|tl|-ng}}}}; [[more]]; [[already]]
#: {{ux|tl|Wala '''nang''' ibang hahanapin pa.|There is no '''more''' else to find.}}
# {{n-g|used to connect adverbs of manner or degree to the word they modify}}
#: {{ux|tl|Tumakbo '''nang''' mabilis ang bata.|The child ran fast.}}
# {{n-g|used to connect repeated verbs}}
#: {{ux|tl|Tumakbo '''nang''' tumakbo ang bata hanggang siya'y napagod.|The child ran and ran until he became tired.}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Nang'' is often confused with {{m|tl|ng}}. According to the ''[https://web.archive.org/web/20200206081352/http://kwf.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/MMP_Full.pdf Manwal sa Masinop na Pagsulat]'' (Manual on Orthography) by the Komisyon sa Wikang Filipino (Commission on the Filipino Language), ''nang'' is used only in the five definitions stated above and ''ng'' is used elsewhere. ''Nang'' is also confused with {{m|tl|na'ng}}, the contraction of {{m|tl|na}} and {{m|tl|ang}}, wherein the apostrophe is often omitted.

====See also====
{{col3|tl|na|na'ng}}

===Preposition===
{{tl-prep|b=+}}

# {{archaic sp|tl|ng}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

