Page 13458 narangha: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|naranja||orange}}, from {{der|tl|ar|نَارَنْج}}, from {{der|tl|fa|نارنگ|tr=nârang}}, ultimately from {{der|tl|sa|नारङ्ग|t=orange tree}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|na|rang|ha}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[orange]] fruit, {{taxfmt|Citrus sinensis|species}}
# {{lb|tl|dated|poetic}} [[orange]] {{q|color/colour}}
#: {{syn|tl|kahel|bulantubig}}

====Usage notes====
* Using '''''narangha''''' to refer to the color may sound old and formal, and mostly used in poetic context. This would probably be the same for {{m|tl|kahel}}, although it does not sound as old as {{m-self|tl|narangha}}.
* Most natives would use the English word {{m|en|orange}} to refer to both the color and the fruit. Some natives may not even know that the Tagalog '''''narangha''''' or ''kahel'' exists.

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|dalandan|dalanghita|naranghada}}

