===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|tl|es|o}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der|tl|en|o}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by the [[Baybayin]] character {{m|tl|ᜂ}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der|tl|es|o}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|letter name}} {{tl-IPA|bullets=0}}
* {{sense|letter name|Filipino alphabet alternative}} {{tl-IPA|ʔow|bullets=0}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|tl|/o/|[o]}}
* {{rhymes|tl|o|ow|s=1}}
* {{hyph|tl|o}}

====Letter====
{{head|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|O|Baybayin spelling|ᜂ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def|tl|letter|17|o|alphabet name={{w|Filipino alphabet}}}}
# {{Latn-def|tl|letter|13|o|alphabet name={{w|Abakada alphabet}}}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def|tl|letter|18|o|alphabet name={{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letters/tl/simple}}

====Noun====
{{head|tl|nouns|Baybayin spelling|ᜂ|f1sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def|tl|name|O|o|nocap=0|dot=,}} ''in the {{w|Filipino alphabet}}.''
# {{Latn-def|tl|name|O|o|nocap=0|dot=,}} ''in the {{w|Abakada alphabet}}.''
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def|tl|name|O|o|nocap=0|dot=,}} ''in the {{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}.''

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|tl|ow}} – ''Filipino alphabet letter''

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letter names/tl/simple}}
* {{l|tl|uo}}

