Page 13959 pa-: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*pa-}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*pa-}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*pa-}}.

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# {{n-g|[[adverbial]] prefix - indicates process of performing the action of the verb}}
#: {{prefex|tl|punta|t1=destination|papunta|t2=be coming/ be going/ be arriving/ be on the way}}
#: {{prefex|tl|tapos|t1=end|patapos|t2=be about to end}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Patapos''' na ang pelikula.|The movie '''is about to end'''.}}
# {{n-g|reduced form of {{m|tl|paki-}} or {{m|tl|magpa-}}}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Patapon''' naman 'to sa basurahan.|Could you '''please throw''' this to the trash can?}}
# {{n-g|noun prefix - indicates an object that is ordered or requested to be processed according to the root word}}
#: {{prefex|tl|dala|t1=carry|padala|t2=remittance/ package [an object that is requested to be brought or sent]}}
#: {{prefex|tl|piging|t1=a banquet|papiging|t2=a banquet that is organized by someone [usually followed by "{{m|tl|ng}} ''organization''" or "{{m|tl|ni}} ''name of person''"]}}
# {{lb|tl|informal}} {{n-g|indication of direction}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Pa'''-Espanya ako.|I'm '''heading''' for Spain.}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}

-------- end text --------
Page 13960 pa- -an: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|pa- -han}}

===Circumfix===
{{tl-head|circumfix|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|causative}}  Object trigger -  have someone do something
#: {{m|tl|pa- -an}} + {{m|tl|bukas||open}} → {{m|tl|pabuksan||to have someone open something}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Pinabuksan''' ko kay papa ang pinto.|I '''had''' dad '''open''' the door.}}
# {{lb|tl|causative}}  Object trigger -  indicates performance of the action of the verb on or to an object
#: {{m|tl|pa- -an}} + {{m|tl|lagay||put}} → {{m|tl|palagyan||to have someone put something somewhere}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Pinalagyan''' ni Maribel ng carpet ang sahig.|Maribel '''had''' someone '''put''' a carpet on the floor.}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally, {{IPAchar|/h/}} is inserted before ''-an'' when the root word ends with a vowel that is not followed by a glottal stop.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|upa|[[paupahan|paupa'''h'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|laki|[[palakihan|palaki'''h'''an]]}}

* Due to [[allophony]], {{IPAchar|/d/}} turns into {{IPAchar|/r/}} when inserted before ''-an'' or after ''pa-''.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|likod|[[palikuran|paliku'''r'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|dami|[[paramihan|pa'''r'''amihan]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|dangal|[[parangalan|pa'''r'''angalan]]}}

====Derived terms====
{{circumfixsee|tl}}

===Further reading===
* https://learningtagalog.com/grammar/verbs/verb_affixes/paan_1.html
* https://learningtagalog.com/grammar/verbs/verb_affixes/paan_2.html
-------- end text --------
