Page 14043 pag-: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*paʀ-}}. Cognate with {{cog|ceb|pag-}}, and {{cog|ms|per-}} and {{cog|id|per-}}.

====Prefix====
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# the act of doing the action expressed by the root; or, the manner in which the action expressed by the root is performed
#: {{prefixusex|tl|gawa|t1=make|paggawa|t2=making}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|basa|t1=read|pagbasa|t2=reading}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The root and the affixed word generally mean the same thing.
*: {{ux|tl|Mabagal ang lakad niya.|He/she walks slowly.|inline=1}}
*: {{ux|tl|Mabagal ang paglakad niya.|He/she walks slowly.|inline=1}}

====Prefix====
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# (''with syllable reduplication'') the act of doing the action expressed by the root repeatedly or habitually
#: {{prefixusex|tl|aral|t1=study|pag-aaral|t2=studying habitually}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|basa|t1=read|pagbabasa|t2=reading habitually}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|tl|pag|t=if}}, which is a {{clipping|tl|kapag|t=if|nocap=1}}, which is a {{clipping|tl|kapagka|t=if|nocap=1}}.

====Prefix====
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# [[when]]; [[at]] (or [[as soon as]]) that time that; [[if]]
#: {{ux|tl|pag-alis nila|when they leave/left|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|tl|pagbalik nila|when they return/returned|inline=1}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{prefixsee|tl}}
-------- end text --------
