Page 14069 Pagadian: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Multiple etymologies exist:
* The city is believed to have been an {{bor|tl|ill|-}} trading post in the past, and so a {{blend|ill||nocap=1}} of {{bor|tl|ill|pagad|t=to wait}} + {{m|ill|padian|t=market}} are widely accepted as the roots of the name.
* Possibly from {{der|tl|syb|gagadian}}, a bird that the native inhabitants call.
* Possibly from the Cebuano word {{m|ceb|pangadyian|t=a place to pray; land of prayers}}, from {{suffix|ceb|pangadyi|-an|t1=prayer}}.
* Also speculated to be derived from {{bor|tl|syb|pengadian|t=school}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|Pagadi7an}}
* {{hyph|tl|Pa|ga|di|an}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=+}}

# {{place|tl|capital city|p/Zamboanga del Sur|c/Philippines|t=Pagadian}}
