Page 14812 pang-: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|pam-||before initials /b/ and /p/, will sometimes remove initial /b/ and /p/}}
* {{alt|tl|pan-||before initials /d/, /s/, /l/ and /t/, will sometimes remove initial /d/, /s/, /l/ and /t/}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*paŋ-}} (cf. {{cog|ceb|pang-}}, {{cog|id|peng-}} and {{cog|ms|peng-}}).

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# ({{n-g|instrumentative prefix}}) {{ngd|forms nouns indicating a tool or an instrument that is used to perform the action expressed by the root}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|tanggal|t1=remove, detach|pantanggal|t2=remover}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|takip|t1=a cover|pantakip|t2=an instrument used to cover something}}
# ({{n-g|adjectival prefix}}) {{ngd|forms relational adjectives indicating use or purpose}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|dalawa|t1=two|pandalawa|t2=for two}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|bahay|t1=house|pambahay|t2=for use at home}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|babae|t1=woman|pambabae|t2=for women}}

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# ({{n-g|Ordinal prefix}}) {{ngd|Used to form ordinal numbers}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|dalawa|t1=two|pangalawa|t2=second}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|walo|t1=eight|pangwalo|t2=eighth}}

====Usage notes====
Tagalog ordinal numbers prefixed with ''pang-'' are usually more informal compared to those prefixed with ''[[ika-]]''

===Prefix===
{{tl-head|prefix|b=+}}

# {{q|with syllable reduplication}} {{ngd|an action or a practice associated with the thing or action expressed by the root}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|gamot|t1=medicine|panggagamot|t2=practice of medicine}}
#: {{prefixusex|tl|anak|t1=child|panganganak|t2=giving birth, delivery}}

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|tl}}
-------- end text --------
Page 14813 pang- -an: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|pam- -an||before root initials ''{{angbr|b}}'' and ''{{angbr|p}}'', will sometimes remove initial ''{{angbr|b}}'' and ''{{angbr|p}}''}}
* {{alt|tl|pan- -an||before root initials ''{{angbr|d}}'', ''{{angbr|s}}'' and ''{{angbr|t}}'', will sometimes remove initial ''{{angbr|d}}'', ''{{angbr|s}}'' and ''{{angbr|t}}''}}
* {{alt|tl|pang- -han||for roots ending in vowels, not followed by glottal stops}}

===Circumfix===
{{tl-head|circumfix|b=+}}

# ({{n-g|instrumentative circumfix}}) {{ngd|used to form nouns indicating a place or concept where the action expressed by the root is performed}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|bili|t1=purchase|pamilihan|t2=market}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|puno|t1=leader|pamunuan|t2=administration}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|tunton|t1=guidance|panuntunan|t2=guideline}}
# ({{n-g|adjectival circumfix}}) {{ngd|used to form adjectives indicating the root is intended for}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|dalawa|t1=two|pangdalawahan|t2=for two}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|matagal|t1=long (of a period of time)|pangmatagalan|t2=for long-term}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally, {{IPAchar|/h/}} is inserted before {{m|tl|-an}} when the root word ends with a vowel that is not followed by a glottal stop.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|bili|[[pamilihan|pamili'''h'''an]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|dalawa|[[pangdalawahan|pangdalawa'''h'''an]]}}

====Derived terms====
{{circumfixsee|tl}}
-------- end text --------
