Page 14979 Parañaque: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|tl|es|Parañaque}}, from earlier ''Palañac'', an earlier Hispanized form of {{der|tl|tl|Palanyag}}, attested in 1582. Of uncertain origin.

A common {{glossary|folk etymology}} is the phrase "Para aqui" (''"Stop here!"''), supposedly said by a Spaniard to a coachman when he wanted to stop in the area.

