Page 15254 payid: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|paid||obsolete}}
* {{alt|tl|palid}}
* {{alt|tl|pawid}}
* {{alt|tl|pair|payir||obsolete}}
* {{alt|tl|pauir||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from elision of {{IPAchar|/l/}} from earlier variant {{m|tl|palid}}, from {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*palij||blow away}}, ultimately from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*palij||blown away by the wind}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|palig}}, {{cog|pam|paid}}, {{cog|hil|palid}}, and {{cog|mrw|palid}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|payíd<a^>|+<qq:obsolete><n^>|new=1}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|payíd|b=+}}

# [[carried]] or [[borne]] by the [[wind]]
#: {{syn|tl|tinangay|napadpad|lumipad|dinala}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|obsolete}}

# act of being [[carried]] by the [[wind]] {{gloss|like [[paper]]}}
#: {{syn|tl|tangay|padpad|lipad|wagayway|dala|wagay|pihaw|q6=obsolete|q7=obsolete}}
# [[get lost|getting lost]] when sailing because of [[strong]] [[wind]]s and [[current]]s
#: {{syn|tl|padpad|pagkawala|pagkaligaw}}

====Usage notes====
* The variant {{m|tl|pawid}} was more used in Manila according to Fr. Domingo de los Santos (1835).

====Derived terms====
