Page 15391 pighati: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{compound|tl|ms:pedih|ms:hati|t1=smarting pain|t2=emotions|lit2=liver}}, meaning "heartache", or literally “smarting liver”. Compare {{cog|jv|ꦥꦿꦶꦲꦠꦶꦤ꧀}}, and {{cog|ms|pedih hati}}, as well as {{noncog|tl|dalamhati}}, {{m|tl|luwalhati}}, {{m|tl|ulohati}}, {{m|tl|lunggati}}, and {{m|tl|salaghati}}. An alternate etymology posits it to be from a [[contracted]] {{blend|tl|lupig|hati|t2=emotions|lit2=liver|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|pighatî}}
* {{hyph|tl|pig|ha|ti}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|pighatî|b=+}}

# [[grief]]; [[sorrow]]
#: {{syn|tl|dalamhati|lumbay|hapis|lungkot}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|dalamhati|luwalhati|ulohati|lunggati|hapdi|atay}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:tl:Potet|TBC|page=87}}
-------- end text --------
