Page 16528 sa: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh-lite|tl|poz-pro|sc=Latn|*sa}}. Compare {{cog-lite|bcl|sa}}, {{cog-lite|ceb|sa}}, {{cog-lite|hil|sa}}, {{cog-lite|war|ha}}, {{cog-lite|tsg|ha}}, and {{cog-lite|gor|ta}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA}}

====Preposition====
{{tl-prep|b=+}}

# {{n-g|indirect object marker}}: [[to]]
#: {{ux|tl|Binigay ko na ang lahat '''sa''' kaibigan ko.|I already gave everything '''to''' my friend.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to refer to the location of something or some action}}: [[in]]; [[at]]; [[on]] {{gl|not used in a positive equational sentence}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Sa''' Pilipinas ako ipinanganak.|I was born '''in''' the Philippines.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|tl|Wala siya '''sa''' opisina.|He's not '''at''' the office.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to refer towards a location}}: [[to]]; [[toward]]
#: {{ux|tl|Pupunta siya '''sa''' sinehan mamaya.|He's going '''to''' the movies later.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to refer to accompaniment}}: [[with]]; [[together]] with; in [[company]] with
#: {{ux|tl|Sumama si Juan '''sa''' tatay niya.|Juan went '''with''' his father.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to refer to a time period}}: [[at]]; [[on]]; [[in]]; [[during]] {{gl|of a year, month, day of the week, time of day, etc.}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Sa''' Lunes kami uuwi.|We're going home '''on''' Monday.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used in comparisons}}: [[than]]
#: {{syn|tl|kaysa}}
#: {{ux|tl|Mas mabilis ang eroplano '''sa''' kotse mo.|The airplane is faster '''than''' your car.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to refer to a place of origin or where one comes from}}: [[from]]; [[of]] {{gl|usually with {{m-lite|tl|galing}} or {{m-lite|tl|tubo}}}}
#: {{ux|tl|Tubo siya '''sa''' Cebu.|He is a native '''from''' Cebu.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|a prescribed point in time when something occurred}}: [[upon]]; [[on]]; at the [[time]] of
#: {{ux|tl|'''Sa''' pagpasok niya sa bahay, tumunog ang telepono.|'''Upon''' his entrance to the house, the telephone rang.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to refer to the cause}}: [[due to]]; [[from]]; [[of]]
#: {{ux|tl|Namatay sila '''sa''' gutom.|They died '''of''' hunger.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to refer to the basis}}: [[on]] the [[basis]] of; [[on]]
#: {{ux|tl|Lumabas ang estudyante '''sa''' pahintulot ng guro.|The student went out '''based on''' the permission from the teacher.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used to refer to one's dependence on or use of}}: [[on]]; [[through]] the [[use]] of
#: {{ux|tl|Nabuhay sila '''sa''' tubig at tinapay lamang.|They lived only '''on''' water and bread.|inline=1}}
# {{n-g|used in combination with other words to form more specific prepositional phrases}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''sa''' pamamagitan ng|by means of|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|tl|mula '''sa'''|from|inline=1}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This is not used with names of people or other living beings, where {{m-lite|tl|kay}} or {{m-lite|tl|kina}} is used instead.
* For positive {{w|equational sentence}}s, to refer to a location of something, {{m-lite|tl|nasa}}, {{m-lite|tl|na kay}}, or {{m-lite|tl|na kina}} is used instead.

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|sa aba ko|sa aba mo|sa bagay|sa kabila ng|sa kabilang banda|sa kabutihang palad|sa kasamaang palad|sa katunayan|sa una|sa wakas|kaysa|nasa|para sa|sa may|ayon sa|laban sa|sa madaling sabi|sa madaling salita}}

=====See also=====
{{tl-markers}}
* {{l-lite|tl|sa-}}

===Etymology 2===
Influenced by Baybayin character {{m|tl|{{tl-bay sc}}}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|name|S|s|dot=,}} ''in the {{w|Abakada alphabet}}.''
#: {{syn-lite|tl|es|ese|q1=in the Filipino alphabet|q2=in the Abecedario}}

=====See also=====
{{col3|tl|sasa}}

