Page 17023 sando: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Possibly of {{der|tl|ja|-}} origin, according to Potet (2016) and the Komisyon sa Wikang Filipino. Compare {{cog|bn|স্যান্ডো গেঞ্জি}}, {{w|Regional_differences_and_dialects_in_Indian_English#Assamese_English|Assamese}} {{cog|en|sando-ganji}}, {{cog|pam|sandu}} and {{cog|hi|सैंडो गंजी}}. Another theory says that the word is named after German vaudeville showman and bodybuilder {{w|Eugene Sandow}} (1867-1925) who wore a sleeveless shirt when showing off his muscles.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|san|do}}

===Noun===
