Page 17063 Santiago: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|es|Santiago||{{w|St. James}}}}.
<br>The {{w|Guan Yu}} sense among {{w|Chinese Filipino}}s is due to a syncretic association of the said deified Chinese general with {{w|James, brother of Jesus|St. James}}, who are both known for their assertiveness and heroism, which non-Chinese and people like {{w|Jose Rizal}} during the 19th century first associated with and/or surmised the Chinese folk deities venerated by {{w|Chinese Filipino}}s on Chinese altars and prints with popular Christian or Muslim figures.<ref>{{cite-book|last=Chu|first=Richard T.|year=2012|title=Chinese and Chinese Mestizos of Manila: Family, Identity, and Culture, 1860s-1930s|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?id=PRewCQAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover&dq=Santiago+Guan+yu&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjahaHCier7AhV9s1YBHQRNCTQQ6AF6BAgFEAI#v=onepage&q=Santiago%20Guan%20yu&f=false|page=191}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|San|ti|a|go|IPA=Santiyago}}

===Proper noun===
{{tl-proper noun|b=Santiyago}}

# {{lb|tl|Biblical character}} [[Saint]] [[James]]
#: {{syn|tl|San Diego}}
# {{lb|tl|Bible}} [[James]] {{gl|book of the New Testament}}
# {{given name|tl|male|from=Spanish|eq1=James}}
# {{surname|tl|common|from=Spanish}}
# {{place|tl|Several <<places>> in the <<c/Philippines>> named after St. James}}:
## {{place|tl|city|p/Isabela|c/Philippines|t=Santiago}}
## {{place|tl|municipality|p/Ilocos Sur|c/Philippines|t=Santiago}}
## {{place|tl|municipality|p/Surigao del Sur|c/Philippines|t=Santiago}}
# {{place|tl|capital city|c/Chile|t1=Santiago|t2=Santiago de Chile}}
# {{lb|tl|Chinese Filipino|Chinese folk religion|Taoism}} [[w:Guan Yu|Guan Yu]] (160-220 AD)

===References===
<references/>

{{C|tl|Books of the Bible}}
