Page 17864 siyam: -------- begin text --------
{{number box|tl}}

===Etymology===
From Proto-Central Philippine ''*siyam'', from {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*siam}}. Cognate with {{cog|ilo|siam}}, {{cog|pam|siam}}, {{cog|bcl|siyam}} and {{cog|ceb|siyam}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|siyám|audio=TL-PH-siyam.ogg|IPA2=si..yám|a2=regional|audio2=Tl-siyam.oga|hmp=Siam}}

===Numeral===
{{tl-num|siyám|b=+}}

# [[nine]]
#: {{syn|tl|nuwebe}}

====Usage notes====
* To describe the quantity of something, the number is placed before the noun and affixed with a '''-ng''' when the word ends with a vowel, and a separate word '''[[na]]''' for a consonant.
*: '''''Isang''' saging, '''dalawang''' pinya''
*: '''''Apat na''' mansanas, '''anim na''' mangga''

====Derived terms====
