Page 18364 tabatsing: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|tabaching}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|tl|tabatsoy|-ing}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+,tabatsíng|new=1}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|+|head2=tabatsíng|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|endearing|or|humorous|sometimes|_|derogatory}} [[chubby]]; [[fat]]; [[obese]]
#: {{syn|tl|mataba|tabatsoy|tabatsingtsing}}
#: {{ant|tl|payat|payatot}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2014|author=A.B. Castueras|title=My Facebook Boyfriend For Real?! Vol. 4|publisher=Psicom Publishing Inc|page=119
|passage='Yan ang gusto ko sa'yo, '''tabachingching''' kong bunso. 'Wag ka na ulit iiyak kung hindi...bubugbugin ko na talaga 'yung taong nagpaiyak sa'yo.
|translation=That's what I like about you, my '''chubby''' youngest child. Don't cry again if not... I'll really beat up the person that made you cry.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2022|author=Jesslie Borbe Unay|title=Do not stand at my grave and cry|publisher=Ukiyoto Publishing|isbn=9789355971340|page=132
|passage="Oo naman iho, ikaw yung '''tabachingching''' dati na kaibigan ng anak ko diba, yung matakaw na bata? Mga dalaga at binata na pala kayo. Kung buhay pa sana si Glezer ay kasing laki niyo na rin sana siya." lumungkot ang mukha ni Aling Glenda.
|t="Yes dear, you're the '''chubby''' friend of my kid back then right, the voracious kid? You guys and girls are bachelors now. If Glezer was still alive, you'd be as old as him/her." Ms. Glenda's face saddened.}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|+|head2=tabatsíng|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|endearing|or|humorous|sometimes|_|derogatory}} [[fat]] [[person]]; [[fatso]]; [[fatty]]
#: {{syn|tl|taba|tabatsoy|tabatsingtsing|tambakol}}
#: {{ant|tl|payat|payatot}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2010|author=Budjoy|title=Kilig Republic 8: Closer You And I|publisher=Psicom Publishing Inc|isbn=978-971-0573-21-9|page=90
|passage=Lahat umedad at nagkaroon ng sari-sariling buhay. Iyong mga inaakala niyang magbubuhay single, may mga asawa't anak na. Ang mga '''tabaching-ching''' nangayayat. Ang mga pangit gumanda, at ang mga gumanda para yatang naging losyang.
|translation=Everyone aged and got their own lives. The ones he/she thought will live life single, already have spouses and children. The '''fatsos''' became emaciated. The ugly became beautiful, and those that became beautiful seem to have become dowdy.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2015|author=Biankee Quinto|title=Bili Mo ‘Ko Coffee|publisher=VIVA PSICOM Publishing Corp|page=118
|passage="Pumayat ka na," I told him. Mataba itong si Collin. As in '''TABACHINGCHING'''. Pero ngayon...
|translation="You got thinner already," I told him. Collin is fat. As in a '''FATSO'''. But now...}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|tabatsingtsing}}

===Further reading===
* [https://www.tagaloglang.com/tabachoy/ “TABACHOY” in ''Tagalog-English Dictionary'', TAGALOG LANG, 2007.]
-------- end text --------
Page 18365 tabatsingtsing: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|tabachingching}}
* {{alt|tl|tabaching-ching}}
* {{alt|tl|tabatsing-tsing}}

===Etymology===
From a final {{reduplication|tl|tabatsing|nocap=1}}, possibly for a humorous effect.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+,tabatsingtsíng|new=1}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|+|head2=tabatsingtsíng|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|endearing|or|humorous|sometimes|_|derogatory}} [[chubby]]; [[fat]]; [[obese]]
#: {{syn|tl|mataba|tabatsoy|tabatsing}}
#: {{ant|tl|payat|payatot}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2014|author=A.B. Castueras|title=My Facebook Boyfriend For Real?! Vol. 4|publisher=Psicom Publishing Inc|page=119
|passage='Yan ang gusto ko sa'yo, '''tabachingching''' kong bunso. 'Wag ka na ulit iiyak kung hindi...bubugbugin ko na talaga 'yung taong nagpaiyak sa'yo.
|translation=That's what I like about you, my '''chubby''' youngest child. Don't cry again if not... I'll really beat up the person that made you cry.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2022|author=Jesslie Borbe Unay|title=Do not stand at my grave and cry|publisher=Ukiyoto Publishing|isbn=9789355971340|page=132
|passage="Oo naman iho, ikaw yung '''tabachingching''' dati na kaibigan ng anak ko diba, yung matakaw na bata? Mga dalaga at binata na pala kayo. Kung buhay pa sana si Glezer ay kasing laki niyo na rin sana siya." lumungkot ang mukha ni Aling Glenda.
|t="Yes dear, you're the '''chubby''' friend of my kid back then right, the voracious kid? You guys and girls are bachelors now. If Glezer was still alive, you'd be as old as him/her." Ms. Glenda's face saddened.}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|+|head2=tabatsingtsíng|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|endearing|or|humorous|sometimes|_|derogatory}} [[fat]] [[person]]; [[fatso]]; [[fatty]]
#: {{syn|tl|taba|tabatsoy|tabatsing|tambakol}}
#: {{ant|tl|payat|payatot}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2010|author=Budjoy|title=Kilig Republic 8: Closer You And I|publisher=Psicom Publishing Inc|isbn=978-971-0573-21-9|page=90
|passage=Lahat umedad at nagkaroon ng sari-sariling buhay. Iyong mga inaakala niyang magbubuhay single, may mga asawa't anak na. Ang mga '''tabaching-ching''' nangayayat. Ang mga pangit gumanda, at ang mga gumanda para yatang naging losyang.
|translation=Everyone aged and got their own lives. The ones he/she thought will live life single, already have spouses and children. The '''fatsos''' became emaciated. The ugly became beautiful, and those that became beautiful seem to have become dowdy.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2015|author=Biankee Quinto|title=Bili Mo ‘Ko Coffee|publisher=VIVA PSICOM Publishing Corp|page=118
|passage="Pumayat ka na," I told him. Mataba itong si Collin. As in '''TABACHINGCHING'''. Pero ngayon...
|translation="You got thinner already," I told him. Collin is fat. As in a '''FATSO'''. But now...}}

===Further reading===
* [https://www.tagaloglang.com/tabachoy/ “TABACHOY” in ''Tagalog-English Dictionary'', TAGALOG LANG, 2007.]
-------- end text --------
Page 18366 tabatsoy: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|tabachoy}}
* {{alt|tl|tabatsuy}}
* {{alt|tl|batsoy}}
* {{alt|tl|tabatchoy}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{suffix|tl|taba|tsoy}}.<ref>{{R:Tagalog Slang Dictionary|137}}</ref> Other possible etymologies include a {{blend|tl|taba|batsoy|nocap=1}}<ref>{{R:Tagalog Slang Dictionary|16}}</ref> and a {{blend|tl|taba|fatso|lang2=en|nocap=1}} {{suffix|tl| |oy}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+,tabatsóy|new=1}}

===Adjective===
{{tl-adj|+|head2=tabatsóy|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|endearing|or|humorous|sometimes|_|derogatory}} [[fat]]; [[obese]]
#: {{syn|tl|mataba|tabatsing|tabatsingtsing}}
#: {{ant|tl|payat|payatot}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2007|author=Arturo B. Rodriguez|title=1001 Ultimate Pilipino Jokes|publisher=Arturo B Rodriguez|isbn=9780967989853|page=201
|passage=Kung mahirap ka lang, ikaw ay pandak, bansot, unano ojabbar. Sa Pilipinas  kung socialite ka, ikaw ay "pleasingly plump." Kapag mahirap ka, ikaw ay mataba, '''tabatsoy''' o lumba-lumba, at pag minamalas ka, baboy. Sa Pilipinas kung  well-off&nbsp;...}}
#* year unknown, Luis P. Gatmaitan, M.D., ''Mga Kwento ni Tito Dok 5: Ha-Ha-Hatsinggg!'', OMF Literature ({{ISBN|9789710096138}})
#*: Nang humatsing ang batang '''tabatsoy''' doon sa waiting shed, nag-aapurang  sumamang palabas ang sangkaterbang virus na tagapagdala ng sipon. Nagpasirko-sirko ang mga ito sa hangin. Lumipad-lipad. Dumayb-dayb. "Ay, ang  sarap&nbsp;...
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1993|author=Alfonso S. Mendoza|title=Iskalper at Iba Pang Kuwento|publisher=Anvil Books|isbn=9789712703164
|passage=Para kayong hindi magkakilala kung kayo'y magkasalubong sa booking office.  Ang pinaka- tsokaran mo na ngayon ay ang hepe, na ngayo'y bundat na ang dyan, '''tabatsoy''', mistulang naging lobo ang gago sa ISKALPER AT IBA PANG&nbsp;...}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|+|head2=tabatsóy|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|endearing|or|humorous|sometimes|_|derogatory}} [[fat]] [[person]]; [[fatso]]
#: {{syn|tl|taba|tabatsing|tabatsingtsing|tambakol}}
#: {{ant|tl|payat|payatot}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1966|title=Philippine Journal of Education
|passage=Dahil dito'y tinutukso siya ng kanyang mga kaklase ng "'''Tabatsoy'''." Magpipista noon sa nayon nina Victor. Naglalakad siyang patungo sa paaralan. Nakasabay niya ang isang pangkat ng mga batang lalaki. "Hoy, Taba!" ang sigaw ng isa.
|translation=He is called a "fatso" by his classmates because of this. A festival will be held in Victor's village. He is walking to school. A group of boys is following him. "Hey, fatso!", one yelled.}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* [https://www.tagaloglang.com/tabachoy/ “TABACHOY” in ''Tagalog-English Dictionary'', TAGALOG LANG, 2007.]
