Page 18540 tahol: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*taqul}}. Compare {{cog|ilo|taul}}, {{cog|pag|taol}}, {{cog|bcl|taol}}, {{cog|ceb|taghol}}, {{cog|hil|taghul}}, {{cog|mrw|taol}}, and {{cog|tsg|tanghul}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|tahól}}
* {{hyph|tl|ta|hol}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|tahól|b=+}}

# [[bark]]; [[barking]] {{gl|of a dog}}
#: {{syn|tl|takin|kahol|aw-aw|q3=childish|kangkang|batok|q5=obsolete or Marinduque}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=2001|title=Philippine Journal of Education
|passage=Ang Buwan Aso kong si Tigre ay '''tahol''' nang '''tahol''' Sa punong kawayang  umaalatiit; Kaya naman pala, ang buwan ay bitog; Tila nasalalak sa naglundong  siit. Ang Manika Noong isang hapon, habang naglalakad, Sa gilid ng daan, ako&#39;y &nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2015|author=Marshall E Gass|title=Maririlag na mga Hagod ng Brotsa|publisher=Xlibris Corporation|isbn=9781499097986
|passage=Hindi ito tahol na galit kundi '''tahol''' ng pagbati. Lumabas si Chris mula sa paliguan  ng sobrang presko at komportable. Hinigop niya ang natitira niyang malamig  nang tsaa. &#39;Kung hindi mo mamasamain, maaari ko bang malaman kung anong&nbsp;...}}
# {{lb|tl|colloquial}} [[fit]] of [[coughing]]
#: {{syn|tl|dalahik}}

====Usage notes====
The word '''''tahol''''' refers to a warning bark for someone unknown or unfamiliar, while {{m|tl|kahol}} refers to a welcoming bark of a dog such as greeting its master or someone familiar. However, this distinction was lost over time and referred to simply the barking of a dog.

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|tahulan|tumahol|patahulin|matahulan|manahol|pananahol|pagtahol}}

====See also====
* {{l|tl|hulhol}}
* {{l|tl|tambaw}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}

{{C|tl|Animal sounds}}
