# {{lb|tl|pejorative}} [[rascal]]; [[scoundrel]]
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2002|author=Frank G. Rivera|title=Mga dula sa magkakaibang midyum|isbn=9789715061865|passage='''TARANTADO'''! KUNG TALAGANG TUNAY NA LALAKI KA, KUNG TALAGANG  IKAW ANG HARI, MAGPAKITA KA! ... '''TARANTADO'''! PUTANG INA MO! Tatamaan  si GREG ng pana sa tuhod. Mapapaluhod siya at gagapang patungo sa mga&nbsp;...|translation='''SCOUNDREL'''! IF YOU’RE REALLY A MAN, IF YOU’RE REALLY THE KING, SHOW YOURSELF! … '''SCOUNDREL'''! F*** YOU! Greg got hit by an arrow at his knee. He knelt down and crawled towards the …}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2000|author=Jose Rey Munsayac|title=Ang aso, ang pulgas, ang bonsai, at ang kolorum|isbn=9789715422338|passage="Aba, talaga palang '''tarantado''' &#39;to. Teka, at kung tanggihan ko ang kondisyon mo  Ento, ano ang gagawin mo, aber, ano ang gagawin mo '''tarantado''' ka!" galit na  galit na si Heneral Pakong. Tumitig nang diretso sa mga mata ni Heneral Pakong &nbsp;...|translation=“Oh my, this is really a '''rascal'''. Hold on, and if I reject your condition, Ento, what will you do, let’s see, what will you do you '''scoundrel'''!” General Pakong said angrily. General Pakong’s eyes stared directly …}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2004|author=Efren R. Abueg|title=Mga kaluluwa sa kumunoy: nobela|isbn=9789715424417
|passage="Sino ka bang '''tarantado''' ka?" Pasigaw ang sagot ni Bayani. Namuyo kay Bayani  ang tingin ni Armando. Alam niyang natitigatig ito sa nakikita nitong kapootan  niya. "Ganyan din ang sinabi mo sa akin noon, Mr. Maglalang. '''Tarantado''' ako.|translation=“Who are you, you '''scoundrel'''?” Bayani answered with a shout. Armando’s view settled down onto Bayani. He new that he was staring at what he saw as someone that he hated. “That’s how you said it to me back then, Mr. Maglalang. I’m a '''scoundrel'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1997|author=Don Pagusara; Erlinda K. Alburo; Resil B. Mojares|title=Dulaang Cebuano|isbn=9789715502672
|passage=Ako? Pascual: Ikaw! Ingka: Ikaw '''tarantado'''...'''tarantado''', '''tarantado''' (Patuloy ang  alitan. Uulit-ulitin ng bawat isa sa kanila ang salitang "loko" at "'''tarantado'''.") Eksena 7 (Sila pa rin at si Dr. Casas) Casas (Mapapadako sa lugar): Ssst...Por  Diyos.|translation=Me? Pascual: You! Ingka: You '''scoundrel'''...'''scoundrel''', '''scoundrel''' (The quarrel continues. Each of them repeatedly says the words “crazy” and “'''scoundrel'''.”) Scene 7 (Still them and Dr. Casas) Casas (going to the place): Ssst…My God.}}
# [[fool]]; [[stupid]] [[person]]; [[moron]]
#: {{syn|tl|bobo|tanga|loko}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2011|author=Emmett Henderson|title=Tagalog Down and Dirty: Filipino Obscenities, Insults, Sex Talk, Drug Slang and Gay Language in The Philippines|publisher=CreateSpace|passage='''Tarantado'''. '''Tarantado''' ka. &lt;Pretty strong insult, but I&#39;ve heard it often. Don&#39;t use it  with anybody you don&#39;t know well.&gt; It&#39;s none of your business.—Walâ ka na roón.  Walâ ka nang pakialam Look to yourself before criticizing others.—Tumingin ka&nbsp;...|translation='''Stupid'''. You’re '''stupid'''. <Pretty strong insult, but I’ve heard it often. Don’t use it with anybody you donmt know well.> It’s none of your business.—You’re not there anymore. You don’t care anymore Look to yourself before criticizing others.—Look at…}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1981|author=Clodualdo Del Mundo|title=Writing for Film
|passage=KANO: '''Tarantado''' ka, hindi mo &#39;ko mahal, &#39;no? BEA: Mahal, siyempre. Binibigyan  mo &#39;ko ng damo, e . . . Shotgun uli! In this scene, Bea and Kano have nothing  better to do. They pass the time away on the rooftop smoking grass. The dialogue &nbsp;...|translation=Kano: You’re a '''fool''', you don’t love me, right? Bea: I love you, of course. You’re giving me weed, e… Shotgun again! In this scene, Bea and Kano have nothing better to do. They pass the time away on the rooftop smoking grass. The dialogue…}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2007|author=Conrado De Quiros|title=Tongues on fire|isbn=9789712719394
|passage=Sa buong paligid natin, marami ang nagsasabing ang maging matino o matuwid  ay bading ang "arrive," ang maging '''tarantado''' o buang ay macho ang dating.  Marami ang nagsasabing ang maging matulungin o mapagkawanggawa ay  square&nbsp;...|translation=in our entire surroundings, many say that being decent or righteous is weak, being a '''moron''' or crazy person is strong. Many say that being helpful or charitable is square…}}

