Page 18998 tatay: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{unc|tl}}. Possibly from the following:

* From {{suffix|tl|[[w:Philippine Spanish|Philippine]] {{der|tl|es|tata||t=daddy}}|-oy|t2=male diminutive suffix}}. Compare {{cog|ay|tata|t=father}}.
* From {{der|tl|nci|tahtli}} <ref name="Alvaina"/> or {{m|nci|tata}}
* From {{inh|tl|map-pro|*tata}}.<ref name="Blust"/> Compare {{cog|lml|tata}}.
* From {{der|tl|nan-hbl|大代|tr=tōa-tāi||elder generation}}.<ref name="Manuel"/> However, Chan-Yap (1980) disagrees as the morphemes were never used in such a combination to mean “father”.<ref name="Chan-Yap"/>

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}
* {{hyph|tl|ta|tay}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}}

# [[father]] {{gl|one's male parent}}
#: {{syn|tl|ama|amang|itay|'tay|tatang|tata|papa}}

