Page 19633 trip: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|tl|en|trip}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|slang}}

# [[plan]]; [[idea]]; [[undertaking]] {{gl|especially on a whim or impulse}}
#: {{syn|tl|balak|idea|plano}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=2008|author=Khavn De La Cruz|title=Ultraviolins|publisher=UP Press|isbn=9789715425742|page=182
|passage=Wala, '''trip''' ko lang, wala lang akong magawa. May reklamo ka? Ako wala. Wala akong pakialam sa yo at sa kung ano mang iniisip mo. Bakit sa SM? Kase. Kase pareho ng initials ko. Yun lang.
|t=Nothing, just my idea, ['coz] I have nothing to do. Any problems? Nothing. I don't mind you and anything you think. Why in SM? Coz. Coz it's the same initials as mine. Just that.}}
# [[something]] one [[like]]s to do {{gl|especially on a whim or impulse}}
#: {{syn|tl|gusto|kasayahan|kursunada}}
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1989|title=National Mid-week
|passage=May asawa at anak ang lalaki, pero '''trip''' niya ang mamboso at mambastos sa telepono. Ginagamit ng lalaki ang ... ang mensahe ng pelikula. Ang problema ay nakaka-depress dahil mahirap labanan nang ganoon ang lalaking sira ang ulo.
|translation=The man has a wife and a son, but he likes to harass and flirt with women on the telephone. The man uses the message of the movie. The problem is depressing because it's difficult to fight such a stupid man.}}
#* {{quote-book|tl|year=1998|author=Honorio Bartolome De Dios|title=Sa Labas Ng Parlor|publisher=University of Philippines Press|isbn=9789715422000
|passage=Siguro nga napapayag mo siya, pero, nilasing mo &#39;yung tao, e. Hindi ko siya nilasing. Pareho kaming lasing n&#39;ung gabing &#39;yun. Arnold, kilala ko ang kumpare ko. Matagal na kaming magkasama niyan. Ang '''trip''' talaga niya 'pag lasing, sex.
|t=You possible enticed her, but, you made the person drunk, don't you? I didn't made her drunk. We're both drunk that night. Arnold, I know my buddies. We've been together for long. What she likes when drunk is to have sex.}}
# [[act]] of [[take advantage|taking advantage]] of someone {{gl|by duping, tricking, cheating, etc.}}
#: {{syn|tl|pananamantala|panloloko}}
# {{l|en|trip}} {{gl|hallucination due to drugs}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|mapagtripan|pagtripan|basagan ng trip|basagin ang trip}}

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tl|badtrip|laptrip}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|food trip|sound trip}}

===Verb===
{{tl-verb|b=+}} {{tlb|tl|slang}}

# {{lb|tl|pseudoverb}} to [[want]]; to [[like]] {{gl|to do something, especially on a whim or impulse}}
#: {{syn|tl|gusto|nais}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Trip''' ko lang na mambasag ng mga bintana ng kotse, kasi sabog ako n'on.|I'ved just wanted to break car windows, 'coz I'm high that time.}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Tagalog Slang Dictionary}}
