Page 19959 turo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|toro||obsolete|Abecedario}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*tulduq}} (doublet of {{cog|phi-pro|*tuduq}}), from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*tuzuq}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*tuzuq}}. Compare {{cog|pam|tuldu}}, {{cog|ceb|tudlo}}, and {{cog|ms|tuju}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA|turò}}
* {{hyph|tl|tu|ro}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|turò|b=+}}

# [[teaching]]; [[guidance]]; [[instruction]]s
# [[act]] of [[teach]]ing {{gl|as to a student}}
#: {{syn|tl|pagtuturo}}
# [[education]]
# [[act]] of [[point]]ing with one's [[finger]]
# [[act]] of [[guide|guiding]] someone to a [[place]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|tl|katuruan|ipaturo|ituro|makaturo|makapagturo|magpaturo|paturo|magturo|maturo|nakapagtuturo|pagtuturo|panturo|panuro|paturuan|tagapaturo|turuan|tagapagturo|hintuturo|maituro|turo-turo|panunuro|taong panuruan|panuruan}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-IPA|turó}}
* {{hyph|tl|tu|ro}}

====Numeral====
{{tl-num|turó|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[ten]]
#: {{syn|tl|sampu|pu}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Fr. Noceda & Fr. Sanlucar (1860) mentioned a series of the first ten numerals, which they said to be used in the ancient times. Numbers in the series from 1-10 were: {{m|tl|isain}}, {{m|tl|duwain}}, {{m|tl|mampat}}, {{m|tl|agyo}}, {{m|tl|tundong}}, {{m|tl|kala}}, {{m|tl|manapit}},  {{m|tl|saga}}, {{m|tl|bulaid}}, and {{m|tl|turo}}. However, according to Blake (1907), the series was hardly possible to be more ancient because the series does not follow the common property of the Malayo-Polynesian family. Furthermore, Brandsetter (1902), thought that Fr. Noceda & Fr. Sanlucar misunderstood, and they represented a series of secret numbers or the numerals of another language.

===Further reading===
* {{R:Pambansang Diksiyonaryo}}
* {{R:Vocabulario de la lengua tagala 1860}}
* {{cite-journal|first=Frank R.|last=Blake|title=Contributions to Comparative Philippine Grammar, II|work=Journal of the American Oriental Society|page=199–253|year=1907|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/592772|volume=28|issn=0003-0279|doi=10.2307/592772}}
* {{cite-book|first=Renward|last=Brandstetter|title=Tagalen und Madagassen: eine sprachvergleichende Darstellung als Orientierung für Ethnographen und Sprachforscher|year=1902|publisher=Geschw. Doleschal, Nachfolger J. Eisenring|url=https://books.google.com.ph/books?redir_esc=y&id=zIIxAQAAMAAJ&q=isain#v=onepage&q&f=false|page=10}}

-------- end text --------
