===Etymology===
From {{bor-lite|tl|es|v}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der-lite|tl|en|v}}.
* Abecedario pronunciation is from {{der-lite|tl|es|v}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyph-lite|tl|v}} <!-- {{hyph|tl|v}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Filipino alphabet}}
** {{IPA-lite|tl|/vi/|[vɪ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|vi}} -->
** {{IPA-lite|tl|/bi/|[bɪ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|bi}} -->
* {{sense-lite|letter name|Abecedario}}
** {{IPA-lite|tl|/ve/|[vɛ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|efe}} -->
** {{IPA-lite|tl|/be/|[bɛ]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|epe}} -->
* {{sense-lite|phoneme}}
** {{IPA-lite|tl|/v/|[v]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|f}} -->
** {{IPA-lite|tl|/b/|[b]}} <!-- {{tl-IPA|p}} -->
* {{rhymes-lite|tl|i|e|s=1|s2=1}}

===Letter===
{{head-lite|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|V|Baybayin spelling|ᜊᜒ|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|24|vi|alphabet name={{w|Filipino alphabet}}}}
# {{lb|tl|historical}} {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|25|ve|alphabet name={{w|Filipino orthography#Adoption of the Latin script|Abecedario}}}}

====Usage notes====
* This letter is mostly used only in proper nouns, unadapted loanwords, or Spanish-based spellings.
* Some purists of Tagalog replace ''v'' in words with {{m|tl|b}}.

