Page 20441 w: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|tl|en|w}}. Each pronunciation has a different source:
* Filipino alphabet pronunciation is influenced by {{der|tl|en|w}}.
* Abakada alphabet pronunciation is influenced by Baybayin character {{m|tl|{{tl-bay sc|wa}}}}.

Formerly, the letter {{m|tl|u}} was used to represent {{IPAchar|/w/}} in the Spanish-based orthography.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|dóbolyu|pre={{sense|letter name|Filipino alphabet}}}}
{{tl-IPA|wa|pre={{sense|letter name|Abakada alphabet}}}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|tl|/w/|[w]}}
* {{rhymes|tl|obolju|a|s1=3|s2=1}}
* {{hyph|tl|w}}

===Letter===
{{head|tl|letters|lower case||upper case|W|Baybayin spelling|{{tl-bay sc|dobolyu}}|f3sc=Tglg|cat2=terms with Baybayin script}}

# {{Latn-def-lite|tl|letter|25|dobolyu|alphabet name={{w|Filipino alphabet}}}}

