Page 20465 wala: -------- begin text --------
{{number box|tl}}

===Etymology 1===
From Proto-Central Philippine ''*wadaq'', from {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*wada||to be, exist}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*wada}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|tl|wla||text messaging}}
* {{alt|tl|ala||colloquial}}
* {{alt|tl|ula||dialectal|colloquial}}
* {{alt|tl|uala||obsolete|Abecedario}}

====Pronunciation====
{{tl-pr|walâ}}

====Adjective====
{{tl-adj|walâ|b=+}}

# [[nothing]]; to [[not]] [[exist]]; [[there is]] [[no]]
#: {{ux|tl|'''Walang''' tao diyan.|'''There's no''' people there.}}
#: {{syn|tl|waley|was|q1=slang, gay slang|q2=gay slang}}
#: {{ant|tl|may|mayroon}}
## not [[in]]; [[missing]]
##: {{ux|tl|'''Wala''' pa sila dito...|They '''aren't''' here yet...}}
##: {{ux|tl|'''Wala''' 'yung kaibigan mo ah.|Your friend '''isn't with''' you, hm.}}
## not [[have|having]]; [[no]]
##: {{ux|tl|'''Wala''' sa akin ang ballpen mo, '''wala''' akong kailangang ibalik sa iyo!|I '''don't have''' your pen, I '''don't''' have to return '''anything''' to you!}}
##: {{ux|tl|'''Wala''' akong pagkain, sa iba ka na lang.|I '''don't have''' food here, go to another person.}}
## [[no]]; I/you/they don't have any; there isn't any
##: {{ux|tl|Ay, '''wala''', hindi ako nakakuha.|Oh, '''I don't have any''', I didn't get to grab any.}}
## [[nothing]]; [[no-one]]
##: {{ux|tl|'''Wala''' 'yun sa akin.|She's '''nothing''' to me.}}
##: {{ux|tl|Ay, '''wala''' 'yun, 'wag mo na lang pansinin.|Oh, they're '''no-one''', don't mind them.}}
##: {{ux|tl|'''Wala'''... hindi 'yan gagana.|'''That's nothing'''... that won't work.}}
# [[free]] {{gl|from}}; [[lacking]]; [[without]]
#: {{syn|tl|ligtas}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} [[break up|broken up]] {{gl|in a relationship}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Wala''' na sila.|They aren't together anymore.}}
# {{lb|tl|euphemistic}} [[dead]]
#: {{syn|tl|patay}}

=====Derived terms=====
