Page 20589 wika: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|'ka|'ika|ika|'eka|eka||clipping}}
* {{alt|tl|uica|vica|vyca||obsolete|Abecedario orthography}}

===Etymology===
Said to be {{bor+|tl|sa|-|nocap=1}}, possibilities are:
* {{cog|sa|जिह्विका​}}, feminine of {{m|sa|जिह्वक​||tongue}}, derived from {{m|sa|जिह्वा|tr=jihvā́||tongue}}, from {{der|tl|iir-pro|*ȷ́iȷ́ʰwáH}}. Possibly from {{cog|ine-pro|*dn̥ǵʰwéh₂s}} and a possible doublet of {{m|tl|lengguwahe}}. {{rfv-etym|tl}}
* {{cog|sa|वाक||sounding; speaking; chattering; murmuring}} or {{cog|sa|वाक्य||speech; saying; assertion; statement; command; words}}, according to Juan Francisco (1963, 1973). Related to {{m|tl|basa}}.
* {{cog|sa|विवेक||consideration; discussion; investigation}}, according to Pardo de Tavera (1887).

Compare also {{noncog|ms|beka}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-IPA|wikà}}
* {{hyph|tl|wi|ka}}

===Noun===
{{tl-noun|wikà|b=+}}

# {{lb|tl|linguistics}} [[language]]
#: {{syn|tl|lengguwahe|salita|lengguwa|ergo|q4=Marinduque}}
#: {{uxi|tl|Ang '''wika''' ng mga Amerikano|The '''language''' of the Americans}}
#: {{uxi|tl|Ang '''wikang''' Tagalog|The Tagalog '''language'''}}
# [[utterance]]; [[statement]]
#: {{syn|tl|sabi|sinabi}}
# {{lb|tl|by extension}} [[insult]]
#: {{syn|tl|insulto|lait|upasala|alipusta|paglait|pag-alipusta|pag-upasala|paghamak}}
# {{lb|tl|obsolete}} [[belief]]; [[thinking]]
#: {{syn|tl|akala}}
#: {{uxi|tl|'''Wika''' ko'y malayo pa ay narito na tayo.|My '''thoughts''' are it's still far but we're already here.}}
#: {{uxi|tl|Maiging '''wika''' iyan.|That's a good '''thought'''.}}

