#: {{syn|tl|uway|palasan|behuko|tumalula|ubakan}}
#: {{ux|tl|'''Yantok''' ang ginagamit sa paggawa ng mesa.|'''Rattan''' is used in making tables.}}
# [[long]] [[stem]] of [[rattan]], usually made into [[cane]]s, [[stick]]s, and [[furniture]] {{gl|such as chairs, tables, etc.}}
# [[strip]]s of [[rattan]], usually used for tying and for [[wickerwork]]
# [[bejuco]]

====Usage notes====
* According to English (1987),<ref>{{R:tl:Leo James English|page=1555}}</ref> {{m|tl|uway}} is used for chairs and beds, '''yantok''' for binding nipa roofing or tying bamboo scaffolding, and {{m|tl|palasan}} is a thick type of rattan. However, these distinctions may not be applicable everywhere, as in some places, '''yantok''' is the plant, {{m|tl|uway}} are rattan strips, and {{m|tl|palasan}} are rattan sticks not made to strips but usually intended to make cane and cane furniture.

====Derived terms====
{{der3|tl|mangyantok|yantukin|kayantukan}}

====See also====
{{col3|tl|uway}}

===Adjective===
